t["npc:agathelos-the-raging"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,353,25.376.0,28.428.0,14.391.0,25.265.0,53.266.0,36.257.0,29.245.0,25.255.0,27.150.0",["h"]="474a0b",["n"]="Agathelos el Furioso",["s"]="Agathelos el Furioso. Agathelos el Furioso es un colosal jabalí acorazado recluido en los túneles espinosos de Horado Rajacieno. Criado por los jabaespines Calavera de la Muerte como máquina de asedio viviente y avatar de su antiguo dios, ha sido empujado a un frenesí violento y antinatural. Su masa colosal y su fuerza lo convierten en una de las bestias más peligrosas que acechan bajo el sur de Los Baldíos. Los jabaespines veneran a todos los porcinos como descendientes de su deidad patrona y progenitor, el dios Agamaggan. Para ellos, los jabalíes de tamaño y tenacidad excepcionales se consideran bendiciones directas de su dios caído. Una bestia del tamaño de Agathelos —que mide aproximadamente el doble que un lagarto del trueno de Los Baldíos— posee una trascendencia espiritual y ceremonial enorme entre las tribus de Rajacieno.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids hold Agamaggan in high esteem as one of the great Ancients who fell during the War of the Ancients; witnessing a sacred boar tortured with bat poison to serve as a siege weapon is an affront to Cenarius's wild balance.",["class:Hunter"]="A hunter can appreciate the sheer predatory bulk of Agathelos, though his twisted, chemically fueled madness marks him as a tragic perversion of natural beasts.",["race:Tauren"]="The earth-attuned tauren know the legends of Agamaggan well, recognizing that the quilboar's corruption of his kindred beasts is another sign of the rot infesting the Barrens."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Agathelos is naturally a massive specimen of swine, which the quilboar revere as a divine blessing of Agamaggan. His unnatural bulk and swollen strength were further enhanced by the Death's Head tribe feeding him potent bat guano to induce a hulking, berserk state.",["al"]={"why is agathelos big","agathelos size","giant boar barrens"},["q"]="Why is Agathelos so huge?"},{["a"]="The bat guano fed to Agathelos drove him completely insane with rage. Because he cannot tell friend from foe, his quilboar wardens must keep him sealed inside a fortified cul-de-sac using magical fields until they are ready to direct his wrath against their enemies.",["al"]={"agathelos barrier","why is agathelos caged","agathelos force field"},["q"]="Why do the quilboar keep him locked behind a barrier?"},{["a"]="Agamaggan is the great boar Ancient and progenitor of the quilboar race. Because of this ancestry, quilboar view all boars as sacred, and gigantic specimens like Agathelos are revered as living embodiments and divine gifts of Agamaggan's enduring bloodline.",["al"]={"agathelos agamaggan","is agathelos a god","agamaggan son"},["q"]="What is his connection to Agamaggan?"},{["a"]="The Death's Head quilboar, the necromantic and fanatical caste embedded within the Razorfen, captured and cultivated Agathelos. They intended to unleash him as a living battering ram against anyone who challenges their dominion over the Barrens.",["al"]={"who made agathelos","who feeds agathelos","agathelos tribe"},["q"]="What tribe created Agathelos?"},{["a"]="The guano produced by the bats nesting in Razorfen Kraul contains hallucinogenic and maddening properties. When fed to Agathelos, it acted as a stimulant that drastically heightened his stamina, aggression, and pain tolerance at the expense of his sanity.",["al"]={"bat guano boar","why feed guano","kraul bat guano"},["q"]="Why was he fed bat guano?"},{["a"]="No. Agathelos is an elite, heavily armored monster whose rage is too deeply rooted in madness and dark sorcery to be brought under a hunter's control.",["al"]={"tame agathelos","can i tame agathelos","hunter agathelos"},["q"]="Can hunters tame Agathelos?"}},["kw"]={"agamaggan","agathelos","boar","death's head","guano","quilboar","raging","razorfen kraul"},["n"]="Agathelos the Raging",["s"]="Agathelos the Raging is a colossal armored boar penned within the thorned tunnels of Razorfen Kraul. Reared by the Death's Head quilboar as a living siege engine and avatar of their ancient god, he has been driven into a violent, unnatural frenzy. His sheer mass and strength make him one of the most dangerous beasts lurking under the southern Barrens.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Quilboar venerate all swine as descendants of their patron deity and progenitor, the god Agamaggan. To them, boars of exceptional size and tenacity are considered direct blessings from their fallen god. A beast the size of Agathelos—standing roughly twice as tall as a Barrens thunder lizard—carries massive spiritual and ceremonial significance among the Razorfen tribes.",["t"]="Avatars of the Great Boar"},{["b"]="The Death's Head tribe, not content to leave Agathelos as merely a sacred icon, actively transformed him into a weapon of war. By force-feeding him the noxious bat guano gathered from the cavern ceilings of the Kraul, his handlers induced a maddened, unending delirium. The foul mixture drastically increased the colossal beast's stamina and fury, transforming him into a rampage waiting to be unleashed upon the tribe's rivals.",["t"]="A Weapon of the Death's Head"},{["b"]="Because Agathelos is completely out of his mind with rage, even his handlers cannot let him roam loose within the Kraul. He is kept trapped in a dead-end tunnel behind an energetic ward maintained by quilboar shamans and guards. Should intruders break past the barrier, they face a beast driven completely wild by chemical madness, growing even more terrifying in size and power when struck.",["t"]="Kept in Chains"}}}}}
t["npc:althea-ebonlocke"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,395,22.466.0,19.393.0,21.423.1,24.219.0,24.274.0,46.167.0,53.265.0,40.235.0,52.228.1",["h"]="c24fc7",["n"]="Althea Cerranegro",["s"]="Althea Cerranegro. La Comandante Althea Cerranegro lidera a la Guardia Nocturna, la asediada guardia local que protege Villa Oscura de los terrores de Bosque del Ocaso. Pariente del alcalde Ello Cerranegro, asume la defensa de una región aislada y abandonada por el ejército regular de Ventormenta. Organiza patrullas, encarga a los aventureros purgar los horrores de la zona y coordina la supervivencia del pueblo frente a constantes amenazas monstruosas. Mientras su pariente, el alcalde Ello Cerranegro, gestiona el gobierno civil en el ayuntamiento, la Comandante Althea dirige la delgada línea de defensa física de Villa Oscura. Cuando Ventormenta no desplegó tropas reales para defender Bosque del Ocaso contra los horrores que acechan, la ciudadanía formó la Guardia Nocturna. Bajo el mando firme e implacable de Althea, estos voluntarios patrullan los caminos envueltos en niebla, impidiendo que no-muertos esqueléticos, lobos feroces y arañas arrasen el perímetro del pueblo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Paladins walking the gloomy roads of Duskwood can assist Althea in putting restless souls to peace, lifting some of the spiritual dread weighing on her militia.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors find in Althea a stern, practical commander who respects martial discipline and values frontline fighters willing to hold the line against overwhelming odds.",["faction:Alliance"]="Althea represents the grim determination of the Alliance's forgotten frontiers, holding the kingdom together where the crown's armies have withdrawn."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Commander Althea Ebonlocke is the leader of the Night Watch, the town militia of Darkshire in Duskwood. She is responsible for organizing the defense of the region against the undead and beasts that lurk in the shadows.",["al"]={"who is althea","commander ebonlocke","who is the night watch commander"},["q"]="Who is Althea Ebonlocke?"},{["a"]="The Night Watch is a volunteer militia raised by the citizens of Darkshire. Because Stormwind has provided virtually no military support to Duskwood, the local townspeople banded together under Althea's leadership to patrol the roads and fight back the horrors of the woods.",["al"]={"what is night watch","who are the night watch","darkshire militia"},["q"]="What is the Night Watch?"},{["a"]="Althea is a relative of Lord Ello Ebonlocke, the mayor of Darkshire. While the mayor governs town affairs from the town hall, Althea commands the militia in the field.",["al"]={"ello ebonlocke relative","is althea ello daughter","althea family"},["q"]="How is Althea related to Mayor Ello Ebonlocke?"},{["a"]="With King Varian Wrynn missing and Stormwind's resources strained, the House of Nobles has largely neglected the kingdom's outer territories. Darkshire receives virtually no soldiers or relief, forcing Althea to depend on local volunteers and freelance adventurers.",["al"]={"why no stormwind guards","stormwind duskwood support","where are the soldiers"},["q"]="Why is Stormwind not helping Althea defend Darkshire?"},{["a"]="Althea offers the core Night Watch questline, dispatching adventurers to hunt wolves, skeletal fiends, and ghouls across Duskwood. She also assists in investigating the Legend of Stalvan and dealing with the wandering terror Mor'Ladim.",["al"]={"althea quests","night watch questline"},["q"]="What quests does Commander Althea offer?"},{["a"]="When the stitched abomination created by Abercrombie marches on Darkshire, Althea sounds the alarm and leads the town's remaining Night Watch guards in a direct, bloody stand to stop the monster before it enters the town square.",["al"]={"althea stitches","who fights stitches","darkshire under attack"},["q"]="What does Althea do when Stitches attacks Darkshire?"}},["kw"]={"althea","commander","darkshire","duskwood","ebonlocke","militia","mor'ladim","night watch","stitches"},["n"]="Althea Ebonlocke",["s"]="Commander Althea Ebonlocke leads the Night Watch, the beleaguered town guard protecting Darkshire from the terrors of Duskwood. A relative of Mayor Ello Ebonlocke, she shoulders the defense of an isolated region abandoned by Stormwind's regular military. She organizes patrols, tasks adventurers with culling local horrors, and coordinates the town's survival against constant monstrous threats.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While her relative, Mayor Ello Ebonlocke, handles civil governance within the town hall, Commander Althea directs Darkshire's thin line of physical defense. When Stormwind failed to deploy royal troops to guard Duskwood against creeping horrors, the citizenry formed the Night Watch. Under Althea's steady, unyielding command, these volunteers patrol the fog-shrouded roads, keeping skeletal undead, ferocious wolves, and spiders from overrunning the town perimeter.",["t"]="Commander of the Watch"},{["b"]="Althea is pragmatic and understands the limits of her militia. Outnumbered and continually bleeding recruits, she freely enlists passing mercenaries and travelers to thin the threats at Darkshire's doorstep. She directs campaigns against the ghouls and skeletons at the tranquil and sorrowful graveyards of the forest, while remaining vigilant against darker rumors stirring deep in the woods.",["t"]="A Town on the Brink"},{["b"]="Beyond common forest vermin, Althea coordinates the investigation and destruction of Duskwood's greatest blights. She assists in unraveling the dark fate of Stalvan Mistmantle and seeks answers to the restless wandering of Mor'Ladim, the fallen knight Morgan Ladimore. When Abercrombie unleashes the monstrous abomination Stitches down the main road, it is Althea who rallies the Watch for Darkshire's desperate last stand.",["t"]="Tragedies of the Wood"}}}}}
t["npc:anastasia-hartwell"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,265,27.449.0,25.445.0,19.409.0,26.228.0,36.156.0,37.159.0,42.244.0,61.110.0,54.148.0",["h"]="7bac69",["n"]="Anastasia Pozovenado",["s"]="Anastasia Pozovenado. Anastasia Pozovenado es una destacada instructora de magos Renegados que reside en el Barrio de la Magia de Entrañas. Guía a taumaturgos novatos y en desarrollo en el dominio de las artes arcanas y supervisa investigaciones mágicas vitales y misiones de campo por todo Lordaeron y más allá. Desde las oscuras y resonantes cámaras del Barrio de la Magia de Entrañas, Anastasia Pozovenado instruye a magos Renegados y de la Horda en la canalización de energías arcanas. Aunque el reino de Lordaeron quedó en ruinas, antiguos practicantes humanos como Anastasia han preservado sus tradiciones eruditas en la no-muerte. Sostiene que la magia exige una disciplina estricta, advirtiendo a cualquier viajero que encuentra que los encantamientos descuidados consumen con rapidez a los inexpertos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Anastasia Hartwell is an essential mentor for Horde mages passing through the Undercity, training higher spell ranks and commissioning vital class quests.",["faction:Horde"]="Through partnerships with trainers like Deino in Orgrimmar, Anastasia bridges Lordaeron's arcane heritage with the broader magical endeavors of the Horde.",["race:Undead"]="She represents the continuation of Dalaran and Lordaeron's esteemed arcane traditions among the Forsaken, preserved even through the tragedy of undeath."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Anastasia Hartwell is a Forsaken mage trainer located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. She teaches spells to developing mages and provides specialized assignments to retrieve arcane artifacts and reagents across Lordaeron.",["al"]={"anastasia hartwell","who is anastasia","hartwell undercity"},["q"]="Who is Anastasia Hartwell?"},{["a"]="She is located in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity, gathered among other arcane practitioners and trainers under the city's vaulted subterranean ceilings.",["al"]={"anastasia hartwell location","where is anastasia hartwell","undercity mage trainer location"},["q"]="Where can I find Anastasia Hartwell?"},{["a"]="She offers cautious advice to non-mage visitors, warning them to be wary of magic as they journey across the world, noting that it readily burns the untrained.",["al"]={"anastasia gossip","anastasia dialogue","hartwell advice"},["q"]="What does Anastasia say to non-mages?"},{["a"]="Anastasia offers various training assignments for mages, including investigating the Balnir Farmstead, exploring ruined alchemist shops for supplies, and liaising with distant teachers such as Deino in Orgrimmar and Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh.",["al"]={"anastasia quests","hartwell tasks","undercity mage quests"},["q"]="What quests does Anastasia Hartwell offer?"},{["a"]="She shares a surname with Andrew Hartwell and Geoffrey Hartwell, but their family relationship is unconfirmed.",["al"]={"hartwell family","andrew hartwell","geoffrey hartwell"},["q"]="Is Anastasia Hartwell related to other Hartwells in Tirisfal?"},{["a"]="She asks mages to gather Balnir Snapdragons so she can measure the spread of the plague in Tirisfal Glades and send the flowers to the apothecaries.",["al"]={"balnir farmstead quest","why balnir farmstead","hartwell balnir"},["q"]="Why does Anastasia send mages to the Balnir Farmstead?"}},["kw"]={"anastasia","balnir","deino","forsaken","hartwell","lordaeron","mage","magic quarter","tabetha","trainer","undercity"},["n"]="Anastasia Hartwell",["s"]="Anastasia Hartwell is a prominent Forsaken mage trainer residing in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. She guides fledgling and developing spellcasters in mastering the arcane arts and oversees vital magical research and field missions across Lordaeron and beyond.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing within the dark, echoing chambers of the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Anastasia Hartwell instructs Forsaken and Horde mages in channeling arcane energies. Though the kingdom of Lordaeron fell to ruin, former human practitioners like Anastasia have preserved their scholarly traditions in undeath. She maintains that magic demands strict discipline, warning any traveler she meets that careless incantations will quickly consume the untrained.",["t"]="Arcane Mastery in the Ruins"},{["b"]="Beyond fundamental spell instruction, Anastasia directs promising students toward vital field investigations. She dispatches mages into Tirisfal Glades, including the blighted grounds of the Balnir Farmstead and ruined alchemist workshops, to recover lost reagents and salvage remnants of forgotten arcane lore. Through her tasks, practitioners learn that securing magical dominance requires braving the hazardous ruins of their former homeland.",["t"]="Field Research and Relics"},{["b"]="Anastasia's connections reach well beyond the borders of Tirisfal. As Horde spellcasters grow in proficiency, she coordinates with fellow trainers in distant lands, such as Deino in Orgrimmar, and directs advanced students toward solitary masters like Tabetha in the swamplands of Dustwallow Marsh. Her guidance ensures that Forsaken mages remain woven into the wider tapestry of the Horde's magical pursuits.",["t"]="Allies of the Craft"}}}}}
t["npc:aramis-hammerhand"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,349,22.484.0,27.466.0,25.181.0,47.225.0,35.122.0,41.202.0,50.214.0,55.193.0",["h"]="c1a012",["n"]="Aramis Manomartillo",["s"]="Aramis Manomartillo. Aramis Manomartillo es un guerrero sagrado no-muerto que se encuentra en el interior de la capilla profanada de Camposanto. Como instructor de paladines Renegado, adiestra a los muertos recién alzados que buscan recuperar su vínculo con la Luz Sagrada. Recorrer este camino en la no-muerte exige una inmensa disciplina, ya que blandir una energía tan radiante inflige un dolor atroz a su carne descompuesta. Erguido entre los sombríos muros de la capilla de Camposanto, Aramis Manomartillo representa una anomalía entre los Renegados recién despertados. En vida, muchos ciudadanos de Lordaeron respondieron a la llamada de la Mano de Plata, solo para perecer cuando la Plaga arrasó el norte. Aramis sobrevivió a la caída solo para ser alzado en la no-muerte; no obstante, optó por no abandonar las enseñanzas marciales y espirituales de su existencia anterior. Ahora ofrece guía a otros que se niegan a renunciar a su devoción.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="For Forsaken paladins, Aramis is the first mentor they meet, guiding them through the agony and spiritual discipline required to wield the Holy Light in an undead vessel.",["race:Undead"]="Aramis demonstrates that rising into undeath does not require abandoning Lordaeron's proud heritage of holy warfare, even if it comes with immense personal suffering."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Aramis Hammerhand is a Forsaken paladin trainer located inside the chapel at Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. He assists newly risen undead who wish to pursue the path of holy combat.",["al"]={"aramis lore","who is hammerhand","deathknell paladin trainer"},["q"]="Who is Aramis Hammerhand?"},{["a"]="Yes, through sheer willpower and conviction, Forsaken can call upon the Holy Light. However, doing so causes immense physical agony, as the radiant energy burns and scours their rotting flesh while healing or bolstering them.",["al"]={"can undead be paladins","how do undead use light","forsaken light"},["q"]="Can the Forsaken actually wield the Holy Light?"},{["a"]="He can be found standing inside the chapel of Deathknell, the introductory settlement for the Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"where is aramis","hammerhand location","paladin trainer deathknell"},["q"]="Where can I find Aramis Hammerhand?"},{["a"]="Aramis offers several class-specific quests for newly risen paladins, including 'A Difficult Path', 'Rediscovering the Light', 'A Light in the Darkness', 'Coming to Terms', and 'Continue Your Training'.",["al"]={"aramis quests","deathknell paladin quests"},["q"]="What quests does Aramis Hammerhand offer?"},{["a"]="Before the plague, Lordaeron was the cradle of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Many of the newly liberated Forsaken remember their oaths and refuse to abandon their sacred calling, regardless of their undead state.",["al"]={"why are there forsaken paladins","forsaken silver hand"},["q"]="Why is a paladin trainer working for the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="While the Light can mend their bodies and grant them martial strength, the process is excruciating. It reignites their sensory nervous systems, forcing them to feel the rot of their own bodies.",["al"]={"does light hurt undead","light healing undead lore"},["q"]="Does using the Light heal the undead in the normal way?"}},["kw"]={"aramis","chapel","deathknell","forsaken","hammerhand","light","paladin","tirisfal","trainer"},["n"]="Aramis Hammerhand",["s"]="Aramis Hammerhand is an undead holy warrior situated within the desecrated chapel of Deathknell. As a Forsaken paladin trainer, he instructs newly risen dead who seek to reclaim their bond with the Holy Light. Walking this path in undeath requires immense discipline, as wielding such radiant energy inflicts agonizing pain upon their decayed flesh.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing within the somber walls of Deathknell's chapel, Aramis Hammerhand represents an anomaly among the recently awakened Forsaken. In life, many citizens of Lordaeron answered the call of the Silver Hand, only to perish when the Scourge swept across the north. Aramis survived the fall only to be raised into undeath, yet he chose not to abandon the martial and spiritual teachings of his former existence. Now, he offers guidance to others who refuse to surrender their devotion.",["t"]="A Beacon in Deathknell"},{["b"]="For an undead being, channeling the Holy Light is an ordeal of supreme willpower. The power burns necrotic flesh and reawakens long-dead nerves to excruciating pain. Aramis instructs his initiates that holding to this faith requires enduring continual torment. Through tasks like 'A Difficult Path' and 'Rediscovering the Light', he demands that young paladins confront the physical and spiritual costs of wielding a force inherently opposed to their present nature.",["t"]="The Agony of the Holy Light"}}}}}
t["npc:arcanist-doan"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,315,21.533.0,21.467.0,23.418.0,37.253.0,53.299.0,36.244.0,35.261.0,42.194.0,38.122.0",["h"]="2a0da7",["n"]="Arcanista Doan",["s"]="Arcanista Doan. El Arcanista Doan es un maestro mago humano que reside en el Ateneo del ala de la Librería del Monasterio Escarlata. Antaño asociado de la Mano de Plata que colaboró en la forja de la legendaria Crematoria, ahora sirve a la Cruzada Escarlata como uno de sus especialistas arcanos más letales y custodio de archivos clave de la cruzada. Antes de que la Cruzada Escarlata se volviera fanática y se aislara, el Arcanista Doan caminaba entre los Caballeros de la Mano de Plata. Durante la Tercera Guerra, se reunió con el Alto Señor Alexandros Mograine y otros fundadores en Costasur. Cuando Mograine reveló un cristal sombrío arrebatado a un brujo orco durante la Segunda Guerra, Doan observó su insólita capacidad para absorber energía sagrada. Uniendo su conocimiento arcano a la magia sagrada de sus compañeros, Doan ayudó a purificar el cristal del Vacío hasta transformarlo en luz radiante, conformando el núcleo del arma conocida como Crematoria.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Doan's mastery of arcane defenses makes his protective bubble a vivid example of magical warding.",["class:Paladin"]="Doan fought beside the founding members of the Silver Hand and was directly involved in purifying the crystal that created the Ashbringer before joining the crusade's descent into zealotry.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces, Doan represents what remains of Lordaeron's proud Kirin Tor and Silver Hand defenders who abandoned reason in favor of the Crusade's violent paranoia.",["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken and their Horde allies see Doan as a dangerous Scarlet commander whose library shelters vital intelligence and keys needed to breach the Crusade's inner sanctums."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Although the Crusade is dominated by zealot paladins and priests, Doan has been allied with its founders since the Silver Hand days. He firmly believes that masterwork arcane magic is an indispensable weapon needed to cleanse the Scourge from Lordaeron.",["al"]={"why is doan a mage","crusade mage","doan magic"},["q"]="Why is a mage in the Scarlet Crusade?"},{["a"]="At a council in Southshore during the Third War, Alexandros Mograine presented an orb of darkness taken from an orc warlock. Doan helped direct the magical experiment where the Silver Hand poured their magic into the relic, successfully purifying it into the radiant core that forged the Ashbringer.",["al"]={"doan ashbringer","did doan make ashbringer","ashbringer crystal"},["q"]="What is Arcanist Doan's connection to the Ashbringer?"},{["a"]="Doan keeps watch over the Monastery's repository of books and historical records in the Athenaeum. Behind him sits a lockbox containing the Scarlet Key, an essential key that opens the locked gates to the Monastery's Armory and Cathedral wings.",["al"]={"what does doan drop","scarlet key","why kill doan"},["q"]="What does Doan guard in the Library?"},{["a"]="Doan blends abjuration and evocation magic. He is famous for casting an Arcane Bubble that renders him invulnerable while he channels a massive, room-engulfing Detonation spell. He also disrupts spellcasters with area silences and polymorphs threats into sheep.",["al"]={"doan spells","doan abilities","arcanist doan bubble"},["q"]="What magic does Doan use in combat?"},{["a"]="Beyond attending the pivotal war councils in Southshore, Doan fought on the front lines at Hearthglen, using catastrophic blizzard spells from the ramparts to break massive undead assault waves.",["al"]={"doan war history","doan hearthglen","where was doan"},["q"]="Where did Doan fight during the Third War?"},{["a"]="Doan serves as an arcanist of the Scarlet Crusade. His private romantic attachments are unrecorded in the Classic sources.",["al"]={"doan dalaran fountain","doan abbendis","doan lore"},["q"]="Does Doan harbor any personal secrets?"}},["kw"]={"arcanist","ashbringer","athenaeum","detonation","doan","hearthglen","library","scarlet key","scarlet monastery"},["n"]="Arcanist Doan",["s"]="Arcanist Doan is a master human mage residing within the Athenaeum of the Scarlet Monastery's Library wing. Formerly an associate of the Silver Hand who assisted in forging the legendary Ashbringer, he now serves the Scarlet Crusade as one of its most lethal arcane specialists and guardian of key crusade archives.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Scarlet Crusade turned inward and zealous, Arcanist Doan walked among the Knights of the Silver Hand. During the Third War, he met with Highlord Alexandros Mograine and other founders at Southshore. When Mograine revealed a shadowy crystal taken from an orc warlock during the Second War, Doan observed its unnatural ability to absorb holy energy. Joining his arcane insight with the holy magic of his peers, Doan helped cleanse the void crystal into radiant light, forming the heart of the weapon known as the Ashbringer.",["t"]="A Mage Among Paladins"},{["b"]="As the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, Doan advocated for total plague containment. When the undead battered Hearthglen's fortifications, he held the ramparts alongside High Inquisitor Isillien. While others urged him to unleash magic immediately, Doan methodically gathered his strength, unleashing a devastating blizzard at the precise moment necessary to shatter the advancing undead ranks. His clinical patience proved his lethal mastery of battlefield evocation.",["t"]="Defense of Hearthglen"},{["b"]="While the fanatical ranks of the Scarlet Crusade lean heavily on martial fury and holy fervor, Doan remained convinced that raw arcane power was essential to purging the Scourge from Lordaeron. Stationed deep inside the Athenaeum of the Monastery's library, he was entrusted as both a lorekeeper and an operational gatekeeper, safeguarding the Scarlet Key that secures crusade sanctuaries across the northern kingdoms.",["t"]="Keeper of the Athenaeum"}}}}}
t["npc:auntie-bernice-stonefield"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="27,445,18.404.0,33.426.1,33.214.0,42.114.0,34.177.0,47.161.0,46.200.1,32.171.0",["h"]="e66a65",["n"]="\"Tía\" Bernice Pedregosa",["s"]="\"Tía\" Bernice Pedregosa. La «Tía» Bernice Pedregosa es una anciana de la familia Pedregosa que reside en su hacienda, en la zona centro-sur de Bosque de Elwynn. Viuda tras la caída de su esposo en combate durante las campañas militares del reino, es famosa en todo el valle por sus célebres pasteles de tripa de cerdo. Se la puede encontrar fuera de la granja junto a La vieja Pedregosa, vigilando con agudeza los alrededores y albergando una profunda desconfianza hacia la familia rival, los Maclure. Como muchas personas de a pie de todo el Reino de Ventormenta, Bernice ha pagado el alto precio de la guerra continua. Habiendo perdido a su esposo en campañas militares, ahora pasa sus días en la hacienda familiar junto a sus parientes, ayudando a gestionar los quehaceres diarios de la granja junto a la matriarca, La vieja Pedregosa. A pesar de su pérdida personal, mantiene a la familia alimentada y el hogar en marcha, ganándose una notable fama local por sus célebres pasteles de tripa de cerdo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Cooking"]="Bernice's pork belly pie is famous across Elwynn Forest as a quintessential staple of hearty human frontier cooking.",["race:Human"]="Bernice embodies the gritty resilience of Stormwind's rural folk, carrying on daily life and family pride after losing a husband to the kingdom's wars."},["faq"]={{["a"]="She is an elder of the Stonefield clan living at the Stonefield Farm in southern Elwynn Forest. She is a war widow who spends her days tending the farm alongside Ma Stonefield and baking her famous pork belly pies.",["al"]={"who is auntie bernice","bernice stonefield lore","stonefield auntie"},["q"]="Who is Auntie Bernice Stonefield?"},{["a"]="Bernice became a widow when her husband was killed during a military campaign fought for the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["al"]={"auntie bernice husband","who was bernice married to","stonefield widow"},["q"]="What happened to Auntie Bernice's husband?"},{["a"]="She is well known throughout the local countryside for her savory pork belly pies, a treat delicious enough that even mischievous neighbors cannot resist bargaining for a slice.",["al"]={"bernice stonefield pie","pork belly pie elwynn"},["q"]="What is Auntie Bernice famous for?"},{["a"]="Bernice suspected Billy Maclure stole her cherished family necklace, stoking the fires of the long-standing family feud between the Stonefields and the Maclures.",["al"]={"billy maclure feud","bernice necklace thief","why does bernice hate billy"},["q"]="Why is Auntie Bernice angry with Billy Maclure?"},{["a"]="Billy found the necklace, but while carrying it, he was chased by the notorious kobold Goldtooth near the Fargodeep Mine and dropped it during his escape. Goldtooth subsequently took possession of it.",["al"]={"did billy steal the necklace","who has the stonefield necklace","goldtooth necklace"},["q"]="Did Billy Maclure actually steal the necklace?"},{["a"]="She can be found standing right outside the main farmhouse on the Stonefield Farm, located south of the road between Goldshire and Westfall, standing beside Ma Stonefield.",["al"]={"auntie bernice location","where is bernice stonefield"},["q"]="Where is Auntie Bernice located?"}},["kw"]={"auntie","bernice","elwynn","goldtooth","maclure","necklace","pork belly pie","stonefield"},["n"]="\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield",["s"]="“Auntie” Bernice Stonefield is an elder of the Stonefield family, residing at their homestead in south-central Elwynn Forest. Widowed after her husband fell in battle during the kingdom's military campaigns, she is renowned throughout the valley for her famous pork belly pies. She can be found outside the farmhouse alongside Ma Stonefield, keeping a sharp eye on the neighborhood and harboring a deep suspicion of the rival Maclure family.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Like many common folk across the Kingdom of Stormwind, Bernice has borne the steep price of ongoing war. Having lost her husband to military campaigns, she now lives out her days on the family homestead with her kin, helping manage daily farm affairs alongside matriarch Ma Stonefield. Despite personal loss, she keeps the household fed and running, earning local fame for her celebrated pork belly pies.",["t"]="A Life of Hardship"},{["b"]="The long-standing bitterness between the Stonefields and the Maclures is a defining part of Bernice's world. When her prized family necklace went missing, she immediately suspected young Billy Maclure of swiping it. However, recovering her keepsake proves more complicated than dealing with a petty neighbor's prank: Billy insists he dropped it while running away from the fearsome kobold Goldtooth over at the Fargodeep Mine.",["t"]="The Feud and the Missing Necklace"}}}}}
t["npc:baine-bloodhoof"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,429,25.664.0,29.574.0,26.551.0,23.242.0,35.176.0,39.276.0,53.220.0,55.239.0,44.219.0",["h"]="58e3f1",["n"]="Baine Pezuña de Sangre",["s"]="Baine Pezuña de Sangre. Baine Pezuña de Sangre es el hijo del gran jefe Cairne Pezuña de Sangre y el protector en funciones de Poblado Pezuña de Sangre en Mulgore. Mientras su padre gobierna las tribus desde las imponentes alturas de Cima del Trueno, Baine supervisa directamente la defensa local, investigando la intrusión de la explotación industrial y defendiendo la zona de los depredadores salvajes. Ejerce como un puente esencial entre los jóvenes bravos tauren y la sabiduría ancestral de su clan. Nacido de Cairne y la difunta Tamaala, Baine pasó su juventud viajando junto a su pueblo nómada antes de que reclamaran las ricas praderas de Mulgore. Sus primeros años estuvieron marcados por la constante amenaza de los clanes de centauros. Poco después de la Tercera Guerra, una partida de guerra de centauros a las órdenes de Khiragg capturó al joven Baine, sumiendo a Cairne en un estupor de dolor que casi desmorona los asentamientos recién fundados. Solo gracias al valor del campeón Rexxar se logró liberar a Baine de su cautiverio. Aquel rescate restauró el espíritu de Cairne, lo que permitió a los tauren alzarse junto a la Horda de Thrall frente a los invasores de Kul Tiras y consolidar su posición en el continente.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Baine respects the spirits above all else, sending travelers to silence dwarven machines and reckless miners before the fury of the earth elementals is unleashed.",["faction:Horde"]="Baine embodies the calm wisdom and quiet martial strength that anchors the tauren within Thrall's Horde, offering guidance to those passing through central Mulgore.",["race:Tauren"]="Baine represents both the honorable lineage of High Chieftain Cairne and the living hope of the young tribes gathered across the plains of Mulgore."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Baine is the only son of Cairne Bloodhoof, the High Chieftain of the tauren tribes. He oversees defense and tribal affairs in Bloodhoof Village, stepping in to direct local braves and protect Mulgore while his father rules from Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"baine lore","who is baine","cairnes son"},["q"]="Who is Baine Bloodhoof?"},{["a"]="Baine stands in Bloodhoof Village, situated in central Mulgore just south of Thunder Bluff. He can be found near the town center organizing tasks for newly arrived adventurers.",["al"]={"baine location","where is baine","baine bloodhoof spot"},["q"]="Where can Baine be found right now?"},{["a"]="Following the Third War, a centaur leader named Khiragg captured Baine, plunging Cairne into debilitating despair. The beastmaster Rexxar sought out Bovan Windtotem's outcasts, tracked the centaur to their encampment, slew the captors, and safely returned Baine to his father.",["al"]={"baine kidnapped","rexxar saves baine","baine captured"},["q"]="How was Baine rescued from the centaur?"},{["a"]="Baine coordinates efforts against the aggressive Palemane gnolls harassing local herds and keeps a close watch on foreign invaders, such as the goblin Venture Company and Alliance dwarven excavators disrupting the earth.",["al"]={"baine quests","what does baine do","bloodhoof village troubles"},["q"]="What problems does Baine manage in Bloodhoof Village?"},{["a"]="Baine believes the violent blasting techniques of the Bael'dun miners harm the spirits of the earth. He seeks to sabotage their industrial tools and scare them off before their reckless digging brings elemental retribution upon the region.",["al"]={"baine dwarves","bael dun mining","dwarf digsite mulgore"},["q"]="What is Baine's stance on the Bael'dun dwarven digsite?"},{["a"]="As Cairne's beloved son and right-hand advisor, Baine already acts as temporary leader whenever Cairne is away from Thunder Bluff. He is widely considered the natural heir to lead the united tauren tribes in the future.",["al"]={"does baine become leader","future high chieftain","cairne heir"},["q"]="Will Baine succeed Cairne as High Chieftain?"}},["kw"]={"baine","bloodhoof","bloodhoof village","cairne","centaur","khiragg","mulgore","palemane","rexxar","thunder bluff"},["n"]="Baine Bloodhoof",["s"]="Baine Bloodhoof is the son of High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof and the acting protector of Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore. While his father governs the tribes from the towering heights of Thunder Bluff, Baine directly oversees local defense, investigating encroaching industrial exploitation and defending against feral predators. He serves as an essential bridge between youthful tauren braves and the ancestral wisdom of his clan.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Born to Cairne and the late Tamaala, Baine spent his youth traveling alongside his nomadic people before they claimed the rich grasslands of Mulgore. His early life was marked by the ever-present threat of the centaur clans. Shortly after the Third War, a centaur warband under Khiragg captured young Baine, plunging Cairne into a grief-stricken stupor that nearly shattered the newly founded settlements. It was only through the courage of the champion Rexxar that Baine was liberated from captivity. That rescue restored Cairne's spirit, allowing the tauren to stand with Thrall's Horde against the invading Kul Tirans and secure their foothold on the continent.",["t"]="Son of the High Chieftain"},{["b"]="Rather than lingering in the relative comfort of the capital mesas, Baine chooses to reside among his kin in Bloodhoof Village. As Cairne advances in age, Baine carries an increasing burden of stewardship, representing the next generation of tauren leadership. He directs braves and visiting allies to combat the unruly Palemane gnolls who pester the borders, and keeps a watchful eye on suspicious outside influences threatening Mulgore's natural balance. Whenever Cairne departs the capital on state affairs, Baine steps forward as the acting leader for the united tribes.",["t"]="Guardian of Bloodhoof Village"},{["b"]="Beyond territorial border clashes, Baine faces modern encroachers unconcerned with spiritual balance. To the east, the goblin Venture Company cuts deep into the sacred landscape, while dwarven prospectors from Bael Modan dig into ancestral soil at the Bael'dun Digsite. Baine advocates for a firm yet measured response: attempting to warn the miners and destroy their destructive equipment rather than rushing into senseless bloodshed. He warns that the dwarves' violent digging is hurting the spirits of the earth, though the miners refuse to listen.",["t"]="Defending the Earth Mother"}}}}}
t["npc:balthule-shadowstrike"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="21,409,22.428.0,19.373.1,29.206.0,39.113.0,46.201.0,28.215.0,51.179.0,46.215.0",["h"]="73d306",["n"]="Balthule Golpesombra",["s"]="Balthule Golpesombra. Balthule Golpesombra es un oteador elfo de la noche apostado en el norte de Costa Oscura, cerca de la Torre de Althalaxx. Ejerce como agente de avanzada para Delgren el Purificador y vigila a los siniestros sectarios y practicantes oscuros que ocupan las antiguas ruinas élficas. A menudo se envía a los aventureros que viajan por la costa norte a buscarlo para ayudar a desentrañar e interrumpir los oscuros rituales que tienen lugar en la torre. Apostado en la espesura justo al oeste de la Torre de Althalaxx, Balthule Golpesombra mantiene una vigilia solitaria y peligrosa. Los confines septentrionales de Costa Oscura están repletos de espíritus inquietos y ruinas sombrías, pero la actividad en torno a la torre supone una amenaza especialmente grave. Balthule actúa bajo las órdenes de Delgren el Purificador, observando los movimientos de los taumaturgos oscuros que se han infiltrado en los antiguos vestigios de los Altonatos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Operating deep in hostile territory right under the noses of dangerous spellcasters, Balthule exemplifies the patience and vigilance of a true elven scout.",["faction:Alliance"]="Balthule serves as an important forward contact for Alliance members sent north from Auberdine to excise the dark cultists operating around the Tower of Althalaxx.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the desecration of ancient Kalimdor ruins by foul cultists is an outrage that Balthule seeks to avenge before the corruption spreads further into their lands."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Balthule Shadowstrike is a night elf scout stationed in northern Darkshore. He acts as an advance scout and agent working in concert with Delgren the Purifier to monitor evil cultist activities in the area.",["al"]={"who is balthule","balthule role","balthule shadowstrike npc"},["q"]="Who is Balthule Shadowstrike?"},{["a"]="He is stationed in northern Darkshore, positioned just west of the ominous Tower of Althalaxx near the coastline.",["al"]={"where is balthule","balthule location","find balthule shadowstrike"},["q"]="Where is Balthule Shadowstrike located?"},{["a"]="He was sent to spy upon the dark spellcasters and cultists who have taken up residence in the Tower of Althalaxx, helping to gather intelligence and coordinate strikes to disrupt their corrupt rituals.",["al"]={"why is balthule here","what does balthule want","althalaxx quest guy"},["q"]="What is his mission at the Tower of Althalaxx?"},{["a"]="Delgren the Purifier is an Argent Dawn paladin stationed at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale who coordinates the campaign against the dark forces plaguing northern Darkshore. Balthule serves as his forward eyes and ears.",["al"]={"who is delgren","balthule superior","delgren connection"},["q"]="Who is Delgren the Purifier?"},{["a"]="The tower and its surrounding grounds are overrun by dark cultists, sorcerers, and summoned demonic or shadowy minions bent on using ancient Highborne power for sinister purposes.",["al"]={"who is in the tower","althalaxx enemies","tower of althalaxx cultists"},["q"]="What kind of enemies occupy the Tower of Althalaxx?"},{["a"]="The Tower of Althalaxx is an ancient elven structure. The presence of foul sorcery and demonic activity so close to elven lands represents a direct threat to the safety of Darkshore and the night elves of Darnassus.",["al"]={"why care about the tower","alliance darkshore presence"},["q"]="Why is the Alliance interested in these ruins?"}},["kw"]={"althalaxx","balthule","cultists","darkshore","delgren","mathystra","purifier","scout","shadowstrike"},["n"]="Balthule Shadowstrike",["s"]="Balthule Shadowstrike is a night elf scout stationed in northern Darkshore near the Tower of Althalaxx. Serving as a forward agent for Delgren the Purifier, he keeps watch over the sinister cultists and dark practitioners occupying the ancient elven ruins. Adventurers traveling along the northern coast are often directed to him to assist in unravelling and disrupting the dark rituals underway at the tower.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched in the wilderness just west of the Tower of Althalaxx, Balthule Shadowstrike maintains a lonely and perilous vigil. Darkshore's northern reaches are thick with restless spirits and shadowed ruins, but the activity around the tower poses a particularly acute threat. Balthule operates under the direction of Delgren the Purifier, observing the movements of dark casters who have crept into the ancient Highborne remnants.",["t"]="A Scout in the Shadows"},{["b"]="The sorcerers and cultists who have claimed the Tower of Althalaxx are engaged in dark, forbidden magic, harvesting artifacts and souls from the surrounding ruins. Balthule relies on traveling Alliance champions to venture into the tower grounds, strike down the cultist leadership, and recover parchment and talismans that reveal the true scope of their summoning efforts.",["t"]="Uncovering the Cult"}}}}}
t["npc:baron-aquanis"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,343,28.422.0,24.380.1,31.268.0,32.324.0,52.368.0,24.268.0,51.328.0,51.293.0",["h"]="ad3b66",["n"]="Barón Aquanis",["s"]="Barón Aquanis. El Barón Aquanis es un poderoso elemental de agua de las inundadas Ruinas del Santuario Lunar en las Cavernas de Brazanegra, donde el Martillo Crepuscular ha establecido su guarida. Emerge de las aguas profundas cuando alguien perturba la piedra de las profundidades de las ruinas. Los chamanes del Anillo de la Tierra lo consideran desde hace tiempo un poder elemental corrompido, y sospechan que la secta está detrás de ello. Sumergida bajo las salas inundadas de las Ruinas del Santuario Lunar, la piedra de las profundidades se encuentra justo delante de las narices de los sectarios del Martillo Crepuscular que ahora ocupan las ruinas. En su interior hay un Núcleo de las profundidades, un artefacto que, leído adecuadamente, revela la historia de toda la actividad elemental a su alrededor. Je'neu Sancrea, del Anillo de la Tierra, envía a aventureros de la Horda a recuperar el núcleo, y perturbar la piedra hace emerger al Barón Aquanis de las profundidades.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="For shamans of the Earthen Ring, Baron Aquanis is a tragic example of elemental perversion, whose tainted remains offer crucial insights into purifying twisted spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="Je'neu Sancrea works with the Horde on Ashenvale's coast, and the fathom core his Horde helpers recover is meant to show what the Twilight's Hammer is doing to the elements there."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Baron Aquanis dwells in the flooded Moonshrine Ruins deep inside Blackfathom Deeps. He doesn't roam the halls: he rises from the water when the ruins' underwater Fathom Stone is disturbed, which Horde adventurers do while recovering its fathom core for Je'neu Sancrea.",["al"]={"aquanis location","where is baron aquanis","how to spawn baron aquanis"},["q"]="Where can I find Baron Aquanis?"},{["a"]="The Strange Water Globe is what Baron Aquanis leaves behind when he is destroyed: an orb that no physical force can break, with putrid water sloshing inside. It seems to have fed the elemental energy. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring wants to study it, believing it will prove what corrupted the baron and how it was done.",["al"]={"strange water globe","aquanis globe","what is the water globe for"},["q"]="What is the Strange Water Globe?"},{["a"]="The Earthen Ring watches over the balance of the elements. Je'neu Sancrea and his comrades have long thought Baron Aquanis a corrupted elemental power, and with the Twilight's Hammer now in the Moonshrine Ruins they fear the cult is coercing the elements to work against the Horde. The baron's remains and the ruins' fathom core could show them what the cult is up to.",["al"]={"why earthen ring care","je'neu sancrea aquanis"},["q"]="Why is the Earthen Ring interested in Baron Aquanis?"},{["a"]="The Fathom Core is an elemental artifact housed within the sunken Fathom Stone. When properly read by a trained shaman, it reveals a comprehensive history of regional elemental activity, exposing whatever dark rituals the Twilight's Hammer are conducting in the ruins.",["al"]={"fathom core lore","what does fathom core do"},["q"]="What is the Fathom Core?"},{["a"]="Not by choice, as far as anyone can tell. The Earthen Ring considers him a corrupted elemental rather than a willing servant, and the Twilight's Hammer cultists who hold the Moonshrine Ruins are the obvious suspects. Je'neu Sancrea says it would be no surprise if they were behind it, but he wants proof before he says for sure.",["al"]={"is aquanis twilight hammer","aquanis cult"},["q"]="Is Baron Aquanis allied with the Twilight's Hammer?"},{["a"]="Not directly. The Fathom Stone, and with it Baron Aquanis, are Je'neu Sancrea's concern: he is an Earthen Ring shaman working with the Horde on Ashenvale's coast, and it is Horde adventurers he sends to recover the fathom core. Alliance explorers in Blackfathom Deeps have other errands there.",["al"]={"can alliance fight aquanis","alliance aquanis quest"},["q"]="Does the Alliance have business with Baron Aquanis?"}},["kw"]={"aquanis","baron aquanis","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","fathom core","fathom stone","je'neu sancrea","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer","water elemental"},["n"]="Baron Aquanis",["s"]="Baron Aquanis is a powerful water elemental of the flooded Moonshrine Ruins in Blackfathom Deeps, where the Twilight's Hammer has made its lair. He rises from the deep water when someone disturbs the ruins' Fathom Stone. The shamans of the Earthen Ring have long thought him a corrupted elemental power, and they suspect the cult is behind it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Submerged beneath the flooded halls of the Moonshrine Ruins, the Fathom Stone lies right under the noses of the Twilight's Hammer cultists who now occupy the ruins. Inside it is a fathom core, a device that, properly read, tells the history of all elemental activity around it. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring sends Horde adventurers to recover the core, and disturbing the stone draws Baron Aquanis up from the depths.",["t"]="Guardian of the Fathom Stone"},{["b"]="The Earthen Ring has long thought of Baron Aquanis as a corrupted elemental power. When he is destroyed, he leaves behind a Strange Water Globe: an impervious orb of putrid, sloshing water that seems to have fed him energy. Je'neu Sancrea believes the globe will prove what corrupted the baron, and how. It would be no surprise to him if it turned out to be the Twilight's Hammer.",["t"]="Corruption of the Depths"}}}}}
t["npc:baron-silverlaine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,378,28.494.0,19.233.0,26.189.0,35.203.0,40.97.0,34.139.0,57.133.0,43.140.0",["h"]="4a3724",["n"]="Barón Filargenta",["s"]="Barón Filargenta. El Barón Filargenta era el legítimo señor humano de la fortaleza antaño conocida como el Torreón Filargenta, encaramada en lo alto sobre la Aldea Piroleña. Cuando el Archimago Arugal desató a los salvajes huargen sobre la región, el barón y su servidumbre fueron masacrados sin piedad. Ahora, su espíritu atormentado vaga por el comedor en ruinas, atado a la no-muerte para defender la misma guarida que se convirtió en su tumba. Antes de que la sombra de las bestias lobo cubriera las colinas del sur de Argénteos, el Barón Filargenta gobernaba sobre una orgullosa hacienda noble. Su fortaleza brindaba seguridad y vigilancia a las tierras gilneanas circundantes. Esa paz se hizo añicos cuando el Archimago Arugal, en busca de un arma contra la desbocada Plaga, desató huargen invocados en la región. Las monstruosidades salvajes no pudieron ser controladas; asaltaron la fortaleza, arrollaron a sus guardias y masacraron al barón junto con toda su familia.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Silverlaine's fate serves as a grim warning of magical recklessness; the summoner's art, when mishandled as Archmage Arugal did, destroys innocent lives and leaves indelible scars.",["race:Human"]="Silverlaine stands as a bitter testament to the downfall of human noble authority on the borders of Gilneas, his family wiped out by the magical hubris of a Dalaran-trained wizard.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken pushing across Silverpine, Silverlaine's specter is merely another remnant of old Gilnean aristocracy that must be cleared to break Arugal's grip on the keep."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He was the noble Gilnean human master of the fortress originally named Keep Silverlaine, situated above Pyrewood Village. He was slain alongside his family when worgen overran the fortress.",["al"]={"baron silverlaine lore","who is silverlaine","who ruled shadowfang"},["q"]="Who was Baron Silverlaine?"},{["a"]="Silverlaine was slaughtered in his own home during the worgen onslaught unleashed by Archmage Arugal. Cursed in death, his ghost remains tethered to the dining hall of his ruined keep, unable to move on.",["al"]={"why is silverlaine a ghost","is silverlaine dead","silverlaine spirit"},["q"]="Why is he haunting Shadowfang Keep?"},{["a"]="His cursed spirit remains within his former home, where he attacks trespassers in the Great Hall.",["al"]={"why does silverlaine attack","silverlaine ghost","silverlaine trespassers"},["q"]="Why does Silverlaine attack trespassers?"},{["a"]="Baron Silverlaine haunts the Great Hall, which served as the keep's lavish dining room before it was wrecked during the fall of his estate.",["al"]={"where is silverlaine","baron silverlaine location","silverlaine dining hall"},["q"]="Where in the keep can he be found?"},{["a"]="It was originally called Keep Silverlaine, named after the baron's noble family who held dominion over it before Arugal took control.",["al"]={"shadowfang original name","keep silverlaine lore","old name of shadowfang"},["q"]="What was Shadowfang Keep called before the worgen attack?"},{["a"]="No. Historical accounts confirm that Baron Silverlaine and his entire family were slaughtered inside the keep when the feral worgen invaded.",["al"]={"silverlaine family","did silverlaines family live","silverlaine heirs"},["q"]="Did anyone in Silverlaine's family survive?"}},["kw"]={"arugal","baron","ghost","great hall","keep","pyrewood","shadowfang","silverlaine","worgen"},["n"]="Baron Silverlaine",["s"]="Baron Silverlaine was the rightful human lord of the fortress once known as Keep Silverlaine, perched high above Pyrewood Village. When Archmage Arugal unleashed the savage worgen upon the region, the baron and his household were mercilessly slaughtered. Now, his tormented spirit lingers in the ruined dining hall, bound in undeath to defend the very lair that became his tomb.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the shadow of the wolf-beasts blanketed the southern hills of Silverpine, Baron Silverlaine ruled over a proud noble estate. His fortress provided safety and oversight to the surrounding Gilnean lands. That peace shattered when Archmage Arugal, seeking a weapon against the rampaging Scourge, unleashed summoned worgen into the region. The feral monstrosities could not be controlled; they stormed the stronghold, overran its guards, and butchered the baron along with his entire family.",["t"]="The Fall of Keep Silverlaine"},{["b"]="Death brought no release to Baron Silverlaine. Bound to the keep's ancient Great Hall, his restless ghost now wanders the trashed dining tables where he once feasted. The cursed lord lashes out at intruders who enter his ruined home.",["t"]="A Tormented Specter"}}}}}
t["npc:baros-alexston"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,316,34.457.0,24.559.1,27.475.1,32.133.0,43.149.0,35.263.0,45.229.0,50.215.1,48.212.0",["h"]="a9ddfe",["n"]="Baros Alexston",["s"]="Baros Alexston. Baros Alexston es el arquitecto jefe de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, apostado dentro del ayuntamiento con vistas a la Plaza de la Catedral. Antiguo miembro de la Hermandad de los Albañiles que ayudó a reconstruir la capital tras la Primera Guerra, optó por aceptar un puesto oficial antes que seguir a su viejo amigo Edwin VanCleef a una rebelión abierta. Baros creció en la Hacienda de Alexston, en las onduladas praderas de Páramos de Poniente. Durante su juventud, unos ladrones asaltaron e incendiaron el hogar de su familia, obligando a su padre a esconder a toda prisa sus reliquias más queridas por los terrenos antes de huir. Con el tiempo, Baros viajó a la capital y se unió a la Hermandad de los Albañiles, dedicando años de extenuante trabajo junto al maestro de hermandad Edwin VanCleef para levantar de nuevo Ventormenta de las cenizas de la Primera Guerra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,1,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="For rogues navigating the shadows of the capital, Baros provides a link to Master Mathias Shaw and SI:7, who hold quiet debts to the architect despite his past ties to VanCleef.",["faction:Alliance"]="Baros Alexston represents the painful compromises made within the Alliance, illustrating how the betrayal of the Stonemasons Guild tore apart craftsmen who poured their lives into rebuilding the capital.",["race:Human"]="Human adventurers from Westfall will recognize Baros's surname from the overgrown, ruined farmstead now overrun by thieves and gnolls."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Baros Alexston is stationed inside Stormwind City Hall, situated right along the northern side of Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",["al"]={"baros alexston location","where is baros alexston","baros stormwind"},["q"]="Where can I find Baros Alexston?"},{["a"]="He serves as the Chief Architect of Stormwind City. He manages the ongoing construction, municipal upkeep, and architectural planning of the capital.",["al"]={"baros job","baros title","what does baros do"},["q"]="What is Baros Alexston's role in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="They were close colleagues in the Stonemasons Guild who labored side by side rebuilding Stormwind after the First War. When the House of Nobles refused to pay the workers, VanCleef led a rebellion, whereas Baros stayed behind to accept the post of City Architect.",["al"]={"baros and vancleef","did baros know edwin","baros stonemasons"},["q"]="How does Baros know Edwin VanCleef?"},{["a"]="Baros held ideological disagreements with the guild's descent into violent revolt. When the House of Nobles offered him the position of City Architect if he refused to follow VanCleef, Baros chose civic order over an outlaw life.",["al"]={"why did baros stay","baros defias split","why did baros betray stonemasons"},["q"]="Why didn't Baros join the Defias Brotherhood?"},{["a"]="Upon Edwin VanCleef's death in the Deadmines, adventurers recover an unsent letter written directly to Baros Alexston, revealing lingering personal resentment and unresolved history between the two former craftsmen.",["al"]={"unsent letter quest","vancleef unsent letter","letter to baros"},["q"]="What is the unsent letter found on Edwin VanCleef?"},{["a"]="Baros grew up on the Alexston Farmstead in Westfall. His family fled after thieves burned the property, and Baros later recruits adventurers to reclaim his childhood possessions, including his very first compass.",["al"]={"alexston farmstead","baros westfall","baros childhood"},["q"]="What is Baros Alexston's connection to Westfall?"}},["kw"]={"alexston","architect","baros","cathedral square","city hall","defias","farmstead","stonemasons","unsent letter","vancleef"},["n"]="Baros Alexston",["s"]="Baros Alexston is the Chief Architect of Stormwind City, stationed within the City Hall overlooking Cathedral Square. A former member of the Stonemasons Guild who helped rebuild the capital after the First War, he chose to accept an official post rather than follow his old friend Edwin VanCleef into open rebellion.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Baros grew up on the Alexston Farmstead in the rolling grasslands of Westfall. During his youth, thieves overran and torched his family's homestead, forcing his father to hurriedly stash their most cherished heirlooms across the grounds before fleeing. Baros eventually journeyed to the capital and joined the Stonemasons Guild, dedicating years of grueling labor alongside Guildmaster Edwin VanCleef to raise Stormwind anew from the ashes of the First War.",["t"]="From the Farmstead to the Scaffold"},{["b"]="When the rebuilding drew to an end, the House of Nobles reneged on the agreed payment, leading to furious protests, the dissolution of the Stonemasons Guild, and deadly street riots. As VanCleef led the disenfranchised artisans into exile to form the Defias Brotherhood, the nobles offered Baros the prestigious position of City Architect on the condition that he disavow the uprising. Harboring ideological disagreements with the guild's path toward violent banditry, Baros accepted the offer, cementing a tragic rift between himself and his former comrades.",["t"]="A Bitter Parting of Ways"},{["b"]="From his desk in City Hall, Baros continues overseeing the maintenance of the capital, carrying political ties that include a discreet favor owed to him by Mathias Shaw of SI:7. Yet his past refuses to stay buried. Following the fall of VanCleef within the depths of the Deadmines, an unsent letter addressed personally to Baros rests upon the Defias leader's corpse—a testament to a bond severed by politics, treason, and the blood shed over Stormwind's foundation stones.",["t"]="The Ghost in the Dead Mines"}}}}}
t["npc:bazil-thredd"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,268,21.547.0,21.583.0,19.469.1,20.238.0,32.271.0,28.322.0,43.240.0,40.273.1,48.237.0",["h"]="46476e",["n"]="Bazil Thredd",["s"]="Bazil Thredd. Bazil Thredd es el lugarteniente y asistente de mayor confianza de Edwin VanCleef, encerrado en las Mazmorras de Ventormenta desde los disturbios de los canteros en los que murió la reina Tiffin. Ahora la prisión se ha sublevado y Thredd lidera el motín de los reclusos Defias desde su bloque de celdas oriental. Cuando la nobleza de Ventormenta se negó a pagar a la Hermandad de los Albañiles por reconstruir la ciudad, Edwin VanCleef rechazó las medidas de apaciguamiento del gobierno e inició una revuelta abierta. Bazil Thredd estuvo al lado de VanCleef como su lugarteniente principal y asistente de mayor confianza. Durante los violentos enfrentamientos posteriores —que provocaron la muerte de la reina Tiffin Wrynn—, Thredd fue capturado por la guardia de la ciudad. Mientras VanCleef y los canteros supervivientes huían a Páramos de Poniente para fundar la Hermandad Defias, Thredd fue arrojado a las profundidades de las Mazmorras de Ventormenta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="A Defias revolt right beneath Stormwind's streets is a direct threat to the capital, and Warden Thelwater wants its leader dealt with before it spreads.",["race:Human"]="Thredd is a living reminder of the Stonemasons' riots that claimed Queen Tiffin and set the Defias Brotherhood against the kingdom."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Bazil Thredd was the right hand of Edwin VanCleef during the Stonemasons' rebellion in Stormwind. Following his capture during the riots that killed Queen Tiffin, he was imprisoned in the Stockade, where he now leads the mutinous inmates.",["al"]={"bazil thredd lore","who is thredd","stockade boss thredd"},["q"]="Who is Bazil Thredd?"},{["a"]="He is located deep inside the Stormwind Stockade, the prison complex beneath the Canal District near the Mage Quarter. At the main hallway intersection, head down the eastern cell block past the ogre brute Hamhock; Thredd commands from the center cell of the far chamber.",["al"]={"where is bazil thredd","thredd location","find bazil thredd"},["q"]="Where can Bazil Thredd be found?"},{["a"]="The inmates have overpowered the guards, opened the cells and taken the prison's halls for themselves. Bazil Thredd, the most important Defias prisoner in the Stockade, has taken command of the rioting bandits and convicts, and Warden Thelwater is struggling to keep the revolt from spilling into the streets of Stormwind.",["al"]={"why are they rioting","stockade riot cause","why did prisoners revolt"},["q"]="Why is the Stockade rioting?"},{["a"]="Warden Thelwater believes the uprising cannot be quelled while Thredd lives to direct it. With the prison guard overwhelmed and the inmates holding the complex, the warden orders Thredd executed to shatter the rebellion's command structure.",["al"]={"why kill thredd","thelwater bounty thredd","head of bazil thredd reason"},["q"]="Why does Warden Thelwater want Thredd dead?"},{["a"]="A quiet man claiming the name Maelik visited Thredd weekly in the months leading up to the uprising. Though Thelwater was suspicious, the visitor held legitimate paperwork, strongly implying Defias sympathizers or corrupt officials inside Stormwind facilitated the contact.",["al"]={"thredd visitor","who is maelik","curious visitor identity"},["q"]="Who was visiting Thredd before the riot?"},{["a"]="Thredd served as Edwin VanCleef's principal lieutenant during the reconstruction of Stormwind and the subsequent labor disputes, helping organize the guild's resistance when the House of Nobles refused to compensate them for their labor.",["al"]={"was thredd a mason","thredd stonemason","stonemason thredd"},["q"]="What was Thredd's role in the Stonemasons Guild?"}},["kw"]={"bazil thredd","defias","defias brotherhood","edwin vancleef","hamhock","maelik","stockade","stonemasons","stormwind stockade","thredd","tiffin wrynn","warden thelwater"},["n"]="Bazil Thredd",["s"]="Bazil Thredd is Edwin VanCleef's lieutenant and most trusted assistant, locked in the Stormwind Stockade since the Stonemasons' riots that killed Queen Tiffin. Now the prison has risen in revolt, and Thredd leads the rioting Defias inmates from its eastern cell block.",["sec"]={{["b"]="When the Stonemasons Guild was refused payment by the nobility of Stormwind for rebuilding the city, Edwin VanCleef rejected government appeasements and sparked open revolt. Bazil Thredd stood at VanCleef's side as his chief lieutenant and most trusted assistant. During the violent clashes that followed—which resulted in the death of Queen Tiffin Wrynn—Thredd was captured by the city guard. While VanCleef and the surviving masons fled into Westfall to form the Defias Brotherhood, Thredd was cast into the depths of the Stormwind Stockade.",["t"]="VanCleef's Lieutenant"},{["b"]="For years, Thredd remained silent and seemingly forsaken behind iron bars. That isolation shattered with a massive prison riot that overran the guards, opening the cells and turning the Stockade into an armed fortress right under the Mage Quarter. Taking leadership of the imprisoned Defias bandits, insurgents, and allied cutthroats, Thredd established his command post in the eastern wing under the guard of an ogre named Hamhock. Warden Thelwater, desperate to restore order before the chaos spills into the city streets, demands Thredd's head to break the rebellion's leadership.",["t"]="The Stockade Uprising"},{["b"]="Warden Thelwater long believed the Brotherhood had abandoned Thredd to rot. However, a few months prior to the uprising, an enigmatic man presenting papers under the name Maelik began visiting Thredd once or twice a week. Despite Thelwater's suspicions, the visitor's documentation proved entirely legitimate. These secretive meetings ended just as the prison erupted into coordinated violence, suggesting that outside hands within the city actively organized the riot.",["t"]="The Curious Visitor"}}}}}
t["npc:bazzalan"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,226,26.332.0,26.349.0,16.116.0,46.155.0,40.212.0,43.166.0,48.197.0,38.209.0",["h"]="664737",["n"]="Bazzalan",["s"]="Bazzalan. Bazzalan es un siniestro pícaro sátiro que acecha en las profundidades volcánicas de Sima Ígnea. Junto a Jergosh el Conjurador, comanda las oscuras actividades del culto Filo Ardiente directamente bajo la capital de la Horda, Orgrimmar. Mientras Thrall se esfuerza por establecer el nuevo hogar de los orcos por todo Durotar, antiguos males se han asentado bajo sus pies. Bazzalan, un astuto pícaro sátiro, se ha aliado con el culto Filo Ardiente en el interior de las serpenteantes cavernas de lava de Sima Ígnea. Rápido y letal con dos hojas gemelas, sirve como uno de los principales comandantes de campo del culto.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Bazzalan displays classic stealth techniques, vicious strikes, and venom-coated blades, making him an opponent of distinct professional interest.",["faction:Horde"]="Bazzalan and his cult pose an intolerable hazard right below Thrall's stronghold, necessitating immediate extermination.",["race:Orc"]="Having fought so hard to escape the clutches of demonic manipulation, Orcs view a satyr directing cultists in their own foundations as an outrage."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Bazzalan is a satyr rogue and co-leader of the Searing Blade cult operating inside Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"bazzalan lore","who is bazzalan","satyr boss rfc"},["q"]="Who is Bazzalan?"},{["a"]="He lurks along the upper ledges of Ragefire Chasm, stationed above Jergosh the Invoker. He can be reached by climbing dark ramps cut into the cavern walls.",["al"]={"bazzalan location","where is bazzalan","find bazzalan"},["q"]="Where can Bazzalan be found in Ragefire Chasm?"},{["a"]="Bazzalan works in concert with the Searing Blade, a demonic cult seeking to undermine the Horde from within. Satyrs are bound to demonic powers and frequently act as instigators and assassins for shadow councils.",["al"]={"why is there a satyr in orgrimmar","why is bazzalan in rfc"},["q"]="What is a satyr doing beneath Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="Bazzalan fights as a classic rogue, striking rapidly with melee weapons, using Sinister Strike, and occasionally afflicting opponents with a mild debilitating poison.",["al"]={"bazzalan abilities","bazzalan attacks","how does bazzalan fight"},["q"]="What abilities does Bazzalan use in combat?"},{["a"]="Bazzalan and Jergosh share leadership of the Searing Blade inside Ragefire Chasm. While Jergosh focuses on invocations and summoning dark forces, Bazzalan acts as the martial and stealth authority.",["al"]={"jergosh and bazzalan","is bazzalan related to jergosh"},["q"]="What is his relationship to Jergosh the Invoker?"},{["a"]="His presence deep beneath the capital represents a direct demonic threat. Horde leaders commission adventurers to infiltrate Ragefire Chasm and eliminate him before the Searing Blade's plot endangers the city.",["al"]={"bazzalan bounty","repel the invasion bazzalan"},["q"]="Why does the Horde want Bazzalan dead?"}},["kw"]={"bazzalan","cultist","jergosh","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","rfc","satyr","searing blade"},["n"]="Bazzalan",["s"]="Bazzalan is a sinister satyr rogue lurking within the volcanic depths of Ragefire Chasm. Alongside Jergosh the Invoker, he commands the dark activities of the Searing Blade cult directly beneath the Horde capital of Orgrimmar.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Thrall works to establish the Orcs' new home across Durotar, ancient evils have found a roost beneath his feet. Bazzalan, a cunning satyr rogue, has allied with the Searing Blade cult inside the winding lava caverns of Ragefire Chasm. Swift and lethal with twin blades, he serves as one of the cult's primary field commanders.",["t"]="A Serpent Beneath the City"},{["b"]="Perched upon a dark volcanic ledge overlooking the central chamber where Jergosh the Invoker conducts demonic rituals, Bazzalan oversees his cultist guards. Like all satyrs, his ultimate loyalty lies with demonic masters, using poisons, fast strikes, and dark stealth to eliminate any Horde scouts who venture too close to the cult's staging ground.",["t"]="Cult Leadership and Deceit"}}}}}
t["npc:bethor-iceshard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,321,27.481.0,23.535.0,36.497.1,23.234.0,35.117.0,46.252.1,34.234.0,39.229.0,47.259.0",["h"]="17fabd",["n"]="Bethor Duroyelo",["s"]="Bethor Duroyelo. Bethor Duroyelo es un poderoso mago Renegado que se encuentra en el Barrio de la Magia de Entrañas. Al presidir a los practicantes de lo arcano y las sombras en el Templo de los Condenados, ostenta una autoridad considerable en el reino de Sylvanas. Bajo su gélido porte se esconde un pasado entrelazado con viejos amigos a los que la Plaga separó. Desde el Templo de los Condenados, Bethor Duroyelo supervisa a quienes practican las artes arcanas y la Magia de las Sombras en Entrañas. Respetado y temido por su intelecto y su férrea determinación, Bethor posee el peso político y mágico necesario para dar instrucciones directas a los magistrados provinciales de Lordaeron. Dirige a agentes de los Renegados para conseguir valiosos grimorios, investigar anomalías arcanas y erradicar poderes rivales que amenacen el dominio de Entrañas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="For Forsaken mages, Bethor represents the pinnacle of perseverance, demonstrating that the arcane arts can thrive even within the cold grasp of undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="Bethor coordinates crucial offensive magic and counter-necromancy operations that protect the Horde's foothold across Lordaeron.",["race:Undead"]="Bethor's personal tragedy mirrors that of many Forsaken: severed from cherished friendships and homes by the Scourge, only to face former allies as bitter enemies."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Bethor Iceshard is a high-ranking Forsaken mage who presides over the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. He coordinates magical research, rogue intelligence, and covert arcane operations on behalf of the Dark Lady.",["al"]={"bethor iceshard","who is bethor","bethor lore"},["q"]="Who is Bethor Iceshard?"},{["a"]="Bethor resides inside the Temple of the Damned, the central structure situated in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.",["al"]={"where is bethor","bethor location","find bethor iceshard"},["q"]="Where can Bethor Iceshard be found?"},{["a"]="Bethor and Gunther were close friends during their days as apprentice mages in Lordaeron. After dying during the Scourge invasion, both eventually broke free from the Lich King's control, and Bethor orchestrated Gunther's recruitment into the Forsaken.",["al"]={"gunther and bethor","gunther arcanus friendship","how does bethor know gunther"},["q"]="What is Bethor's history with Gunther Arcanus?"},{["a"]="Thule Ravenclaw was the third member of Bethor and Gunther's apprentice circle. Unlike the other two, Thule willingly pledged his soul to the Lich King during the Scourge invasion, becoming a hated necromancer residing at Fenris Isle.",["al"]={"thule ravenclaw connection","thule and bethor","bethor ravenclaw"},["q"]="Who was Thule Ravenclaw to Bethor?"},{["a"]="In their youth, Bethor, Gunther, and Thule wove their practice wands together as a symbol of their eternal friendship. That braided keepsake remains a poignant artifact tying the three fractured spellcasters to their mortal past.",["al"]={"woven wand","wand to bethor","bethor apprentice wand"},["q"]="What is the story behind Bethor's wand?"},{["a"]="Bethor serves as one of the leading arcane authorities in the Undercity. He guides newly risen magi and warlocks, directs military intelligence regarding rogue necromancers, and holds authority over regional Forsaken civil officials such as magistrate Sevren.",["al"]={"bethor role","what does bethor do","bethor authority"},["q"]="What role does Bethor play in Forsaken society?"}},["kw"]={"bethor iceshard","forsaken","gunther arcanus","magic quarter","prodigal lich","temple of the damned","thule ravenclaw","undercity"},["n"]="Bethor Iceshard",["s"]="Bethor Iceshard is a powerful Forsaken mage based in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity. Presiding over the arcane and shadow practitioners within the Temple of the Damned, he commands considerable authority in Sylvanas's realm. Beneath his chilly demeanor lies a past entwined with old friends torn apart by the Scourge.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing within the Temple of the Damned, Bethor Iceshard oversees the practitioners of the arcane arts and shadow magic in the Undercity. Respected and feared for his intellect and icy resolve, Bethor wields sufficient political and magical weight to give direct instructions to provincial magistrates across Lordaeron. He directs agents of the Forsaken to secure valuable grimoires, investigate arcane anomalies, and stamp out rival powers that threaten the Undercity's dominion.",["t"]="Master of the Magic Quarter"},{["b"]="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, Bethor was a mortal apprentice studying magic alongside two close companions: Gunther Arcanus and Thule Ravenclaw. As a testament to their fellowship, the three students wove their practice wands together. The Scourge shattered that bond entirely. When death and dark magic swept across the kingdom, Thule Ravenclaw willfully surrendered his soul to the Lich King, Gunther perished and rose on an isolated island in Brightwater Lake, and Bethor succumbed only to later break free as Forsaken.",["t"]="Bonds of Apprenticehood"},{["b"]="Bethor has not forgotten his former companions. Tracking down powerful undead spellcasters throughout Tirisfal and Silverpine, he dispatches agents to discern whether rogue practitioners serve the Lich King or might be turned toward the Forsaken cause. When Bethor identifies Gunther Arcanus raising the dead on Brightwater Lake, he works patiently to bring his old friend into Lady Sylvanas's fold, while offering no mercy to Thule Ravenclaw, whose willing betrayal doomed their past brotherhood.",["t"]="Old Friends and Bittersweet Reunions"}}}}}
t["npc:billy-maclure"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,336,22.504.0,19.617.1,21.202.0,33.160.0,36.147.0,42.197.1,62.209.1,17.209.1",["h"]="acbb1e",["n"]="Billy Maclure",["s"]="Billy Maclure. Billy Maclure es un travieso muchacho humano que vive en Los Viñedos de Maclure, en el Bosque de Elwynn. En medio de una amarga disputa entre su familia y los vecinos Stonefield, las mezquinas travesuras de Billy suelen causar problemas a ambas granjas. Su debilidad por los pasteles recién hechos facilita sobornarlo cuando sus fechorías se le van de las manos. Por lo general, se puede encontrar a Billy Maclure holgazaneando fuera del granero en Los Viñedos de Maclure, no lejos del granjero Gerard Tiller. Criado entre hileras interminables de vides, Billy pasa gran parte de su tiempo eludiendo las tareas y correteando por los prados rurales del centro del Bosque de Elwynn. Al igual que el resto de su familia, es muy consciente de la prolongada hostilidad entre los Maclure y los Stonefield, aunque Billy se toma la disputa más bien como un juego de bromas y pequeños hurtos que como un conflicto serio.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,1,1,1},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers newly arrived from Northshire, assisting with Billy's foolish pranks provides an introduction to the dangers lurking in Fargodeep Mine.",["profession:Cooking"]="Auntie Bernice's renowned pork belly pie demonstrates how simple frontier cooking can resolve tense local disputes and pry confessions from tight-lipped farm boys.",["race:Human"]="Billy represents the grounded, everyday squabbles of the Elwynn countryside, showing that even with Stormwind's political turmoil, local farm feuds and childhood misbehavior carry on as usual."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Billy Maclure is a young human child living at the Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest. He spends his days dodging work around the farm, playing pranks, and aggravating the neighboring Stonefield family.",["al"]={"who is billy","billy maclure lore","maclure kid"},["q"]="Who is Billy Maclure?"},{["a"]="Billy is stationed just outside the main barn on the grounds of the Maclure Vineyards, located in central Elwynn Forest to the southwest of the Stonefield Farm.",["al"]={"billy maclure location","where is billy","find billy maclure"},["q"]="Where can Billy Maclure be found?"},{["a"]="Billy snuck over to the Stonefield Farm and stole Auntie Bernice Stonefield's heirloom necklace as part of the ongoing feud between their families.",["al"]={"bernice necklace","what did billy steal","stolen necklace elwynn"},["q"]="What did Billy do to Auntie Bernice?"},{["a"]="While playing carelessly near the entrance of Fargodeep Mine, Billy dropped the necklace. It was swiftly picked up by Goldtooth, a notorious and formidable kobold who carried it deep into the mine.",["al"]={"where is the necklace","lost necklace elwynn","who has bernice necklace"},["q"]="What happened to the necklace Billy stole?"},{["a"]="Billy refuses to tell the truth out of stubbornness and fear of punishment, but he cannot resist his appetite. Offering him one of Auntie Bernice's freshly baked pork belly pies is enough to loosen his tongue.",["al"]={"pie for billy","how to bribe billy","bribing billy maclure"},["q"]="How do you get Billy to confess what happened to the necklace?"},{["a"]="Goldtooth is an exceptionally large and vicious kobold leader who nests inside Fargodeep Mine. He snatched Auntie Bernice's dropped necklace from near the mine's entrance and hoards it within the dark tunnels.",["al"]={"who is goldtooth","goldtooth lore","fargodeep kobold"},["q"]="Who is Goldtooth?"}},["kw"]={"bernice stonefield","billy maclure","fargodeep mine","goldtooth","lost necklace","maclure vineyards","pork belly pie","stonefield"},["n"]="Billy Maclure",["s"]="Billy Maclure is a mischievous young human boy living at the Maclure Vineyards in Elwynn Forest. Caught in the midst of a bitter feud between his family and the neighboring Stonefields, Billy's petty antics often cause trouble for both farms. His weakness for fresh pastries makes him easy to bribe when his shenanigans get out of hand.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Billy Maclure can usually be found loitering outside the barn at the Maclure Vineyards, not far from the farmer Gerard Tiller. Growing up amidst the endless rows of grapevines, Billy spends much of his time dodging chores and running wild across the rural meadows of central Elwynn Forest. Like the rest of his kin, he is keenly aware of the long-standing hostility between the Maclures and the Stonefields, though Billy treats the feud more like a game of pranks and petty theft than a serious conflict.",["t"]="A Boy at the Vineyards"},{["b"]="Billy's mischief crossed the line when he swiped a treasured heirloom necklace belonging to Auntie Bernice Stonefield. While dashing about near the perilous Fargodeep Mine, the frightened youngster lost his grip on the trinket. Before he could retrieve it, the necklace was snatched up by a particularly massive and vicious kobold named Goldtooth, who vanished back into the subterranean tunnels. Terrified of both the subterranean vermin and the wrath of the neighboring elders, Billy remains reluctant to confess until coaxed with a savory bribe—specifically, a hot pork belly pie baked by Auntie Bernice herself.",["t"]="The Stolen Necklace"}}}}}
t["npc:blind-hunter"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,212,19.390.0,13.376.0,25.200.0,35.134.0,35.203.0,34.163.0,30.169.0,43.209.0",["h"]="f66a73",["n"]="Cazador ciego",["s"]="Cazador ciego. El Cazador ciego es un esquivo murciélago albino que anida en las profundidades de Horado Rajacieno. A diferencia de los murciélagos ordinarios que anidan cerca de las entradas de las cavernas, esta criatura poco común merodea por las profundidades sin sol del reducto de los jabaespines. Horado Rajacieno está repleto de zarzales serpenteantes y oscuras cavernas subterráneas. Mientras que los murciélagos comunes del Horado anidan más cerca de la superficie, donde se filtra una tenue luz del mundo exterior, el Cazador ciego se ha adaptado por completo a los recovecos más lejanos y oscuros de la maleza. Su piel pálida y albina y su mirada lechosa son probablemente el resultado de generaciones pasadas en total aislamiento de la luz solar natural.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="For beastmasters traversing the Barrens, the Blind Hunter represents a prize quarry—either as a rare albino beast to tame or as a source of well-crafted subterranean bows."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Blind Hunter is a rare albino bat dwelling in the deepest, pitch-black tunnels of Razorfen Kraul. It is remarkably pale and elusive compared to the common cavern bats found closer to the entrance.",["al"]={"who is blind hunter","what is blind hunter","blind hunter bat"},["q"]="What is the Blind Hunter?"},{["a"]="It dwells in the shadowy interior paths of Razorfen Kraul, nesting well past the threshold where outside daylight fades away entirely.",["al"]={"blind hunter location","where to find blind hunter","blind hunter spawn"},["q"]="Where does the Blind Hunter appear?"},{["a"]="While naturalists and adventurers suspect it is truly blind due to its milky eyes and deep-cave habitat, its hunting ability remains razor-sharp, relying on keen hearing and echolocation in the darkness.",["al"]={"is it blind","can blind hunter see"},["q"]="Is the Blind Hunter actually blind?"},{["a"]="Yes, beastmasters capable of managing winged predators can tame the Blind Hunter, making it a distinctive pale companion for those patient enough to track it down.",["al"]={"can i tame blind hunter","blind hunter tameable","blind hunter pet"},["q"]="Can hunters tame the Blind Hunter?"},{["a"]="It is an albino specimen whose coloration likely developed from living in perpetual darkness far from the reach of the sun, unlike bats that venture near the cave mouth.",["al"]={"why is it albino","why is blind hunter white","albino bat"},["q"]="Why is the Blind Hunter white?"},{["a"]="Ordinary Kraul bats possess typical dark coloration and live nearer to the entrance where light still penetrates, whereas the Blind Hunter is pale, reclusive, and adapted strictly to deep subterranean tunnels.",["al"]={"kraul bat difference","kraul bat vs blind hunter"},["q"]="How does it differ from regular Kraul bats?"}},["kw"]={"albino bat","blind hunter","kraul bat","kraul beast","rare bat","razorfen kraul"},["n"]="Blind Hunter",["s"]="The Blind Hunter is an elusive, albino bat that roosts deep within Razorfen Kraul. Unlike the ordinary bats nesting near the cavern entrances, this rare creature prowls the sunless depths of the quilboar redoubt.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Razorfen Kraul is riddled with winding briars and dark subterranean caverns. While common Kraul bats roost nearer to the surface where faint light filters in from the outside world, the Blind Hunter has adapted entirely to the furthest, darkest alcoves of the tangle. Its pale, albino hide and milky gaze are likely the result of generations spent completely isolated from natural sunlight.",["t"]="Depths of the Kraul"},{["b"]="True to its name, scholars and scouts believe the creature has lost most or all of its conventional eyesight, relying instead on keen senses of hearing and echolocation to track prey through the gloom. It rarely shows itself, appearing only on occasion to hunt through the dense thickets, making an encounter with this phantom beast a prized occurrence among cavern explorers.",["t"]="A Rare Quarry"}}}}}
t["npc:blind-mary"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,265,15.415.0,18.434.0,18.232.0,29.171.0,28.141.0,42.210.0,38.165.0,39.262.0",["h"]="41d1c8",["n"]="Mary la Ciega",["s"]="Mary la Ciega. Mary la Ciega es un alma en pena atormentada que ronda una granja ruinosa y abandonada justo al sureste de Villa Oscura, en el Bosque del Ocaso. Antaño una mujer mortal hermosa y vanidosa, su violenta muerte y transformación la empujaron a la automutilación debido al dolor por aquello en lo que se había convertido. Antes de que las sombras se cernieran sobre el Bosque del Ocaso, Mary era conocida como una llamativa mujer mortal que se enorgullecía enormemente de su belleza y a la que rara vez se veía sin su preciado espejo. Cuando los no-muertos asolaron la región, Mary fue asesinada junto con muchos de sus vecinos. A diferencia de aquellos que hallaron descanso en la tierra, su espíritu perduró como una etérea alma en pena, condenada a vagar por el reino mortal en una forma fantasmal y traslúcida.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="Mary represents a tragic example of a soul untethered by horrific trauma, caught halfway between life and damnation through grief and vanity.",["faction:Alliance"]="Blind Mary's tragic fate is an intimate reminder for Darkshire's defenders of how deeply the curse of Duskwood has devastated everyday townsfolk.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Artisans of the loom occasionally seek out spectral entities like Mary for ghost hair thread, a delicate and supernatural material woven from ethereal remnants."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Blind Mary is a banshee haunting a ruined homestead on the southeastern outskirts of Darkshire. In life, she was a beautiful local woman, but she was slaughtered during Duskwood's descent into darkness and arose as an undead spirit.",["al"]={"who is blind mary","blind mary backstory","blind mary lore","blind mary duskwood"},["q"]="Who is Blind Mary?"},{["a"]="Consumed by grief and despair over her horrific banshee form, Mary clawed her own eyes out with her bare hands so she would never have to witness her own reflection again.",["al"]={"why is she blind","how did blind mary lose her eyes","blind mary eyes"},["q"]="Why is she called Blind Mary?"},{["a"]="She lingers inside a dilapidated farmhouse known as Blind Mary's Haunt, situated just southeast of the town of Darkshire in eastern Duskwood.",["al"]={"blind mary location","where is blind mary","blind mary haunt"},["q"]="Where does Blind Mary dwell?"},{["a"]="Unlike the aggressive ghouls and skeletons wandering the surrounding woods, Blind Mary does not immediately attack travelers. She remains trapped in mourning and can be spoken to by those who approach her ruin.",["al"]={"is blind mary hostile","does blind mary attack","can you talk to blind mary"},["q"]="Is Blind Mary hostile to living travelers?"},{["a"]="After tearing out her eyes in horror at her spectral state, Mary cast away her prized looking glass, leaving it lost somewhere among the haunted reaches of Duskwood.",["al"]={"mary mirror","blind mary looking glass","what happened to her mirror"},["q"]="What happened to Mary's looking glass?"},{["a"]="Travelers and local artisans visit Mary during tasks around Darkshire, whether seeking to recover long-lost items like her discarded mirror, gathering ghost hair for specialized stitching, or returning forgotten personal keepsakes to soothe her tormented spirit.",["al"]={"blind mary quests","why visit blind mary","blind mary questline"},["q"]="Why do adventurers seek out Blind Mary?"}},["kw"]={"banshee","blind mary","darkshire","duskwood","ghost hair","haunt","looking glass","wraith"},["n"]="Blind Mary",["s"]="Blind Mary is a tormented banshee haunting an abandoned, ruined farmhouse just southeast of Darkshire in Duskwood. Once a vain and beautiful mortal woman, her violent death and transformation drove her to self-inflicted mutilation in grief over what she had become.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the shadows fell across Duskwood, Mary was known as a striking mortal woman who took immense pride in her beauty, rarely seen without her treasured looking glass. When the undead swept over the region, Mary was slain along with many of her neighbors. Unlike those who found rest in the earth, her spirit lingered on as an ethereal banshee, condemned to wander the mortal realm in a ghastly, translucent form.",["t"]="A Tragic Vanity"},{["b"]="Awakening to undeath, Mary was overwhelmed by sorrow, horror, and fury at her monstrous reflection. Incapable of enduring the sight of her spectral visage, she clawed out her own eyes with her bare hands so she would never gaze upon herself again. In her agony, she discarded her beloved looking glass, leaving her to drift through her abandoned home as a blind, weeping wraith clutching to faint memories of the mortal life she lost.",["t"]="Blinded by Despair"}}}}}
t["npc:bolvar-fordragon"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,433,19.604.0,15.612.1,44.334.0,60.380.0,56.284.0,51.271.0",["h"]="53443b",["n"]="Bolvar Fordragón",["s"]="Bolvar Fordragón. El Alto Señor Bolvar Fordragón ejerce de regente de Ventormenta y comandante supremo de sus fuerzas armadas tras la misteriosa desaparición del rey Varian Wrynn. Junto al joven rey niño Anduin Wrynn en el Castillo de Ventormenta, se esfuerza por mantener unido el reino en medio de una creciente agitación interna. Aunque profundamente honorable, Bolvar a menudo ve sus decisiones marciales influenciadas y paralizadas por la consejera real Lady Katrana Prestor. Cuando el rey Varian desapareció de camino a una cumbre de paz en Isla Theramore, Ventormenta se vio sumida en el caos político. El príncipe Anduin, de diez años, fue coronado para mantener la continuidad, pero el verdadero poder de gobierno recayó en el Alto Señor Bolvar Fordragón como regente. Bolvar es un venerado paladín consagrado a la corona, pero se enfrenta a una inmensa tensión. El ejército de Ventormenta se encuentra disperso por Páramos de Poniente, Montañas Crestagrana y Bosque del Ocaso. Para agravar estas crisis, Bolvar acata con frecuencia el consejo de Lady Katrana Prestor, cuyas opiniones desdeñosas le impiden de forma constante destinar tropas reales a las poblaciones periféricas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Bolvar represents the pinnacle of the Alliance's martial paladins, embodying steadfast devotion to the Light and unyielding duty to his people despite mounting political subterfuge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As Supreme Commander of Stormwind, Bolvar is the administrative head of the human military, balancing localized rebellions with broader Alliance obligations."},["faq"]={{["a"]="King Varian Wrynn disappeared under suspicious circumstances while traveling by ship to a diplomatic summit at Theramore Isle. In his absence, Varian's ten-year-old son Anduin was crowned king to preserve political order, while Highlord Bolvar was appointed Regent to govern the kingdom and command its armies until the king is found.",["al"]={"where is the king","why is bolvar in charge","who is the regent"},["q"]="Why is Bolvar ruling instead of King Varian?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's standing armies are stretched thin guarding the core territories and borders. Furthermore, Bolvar's chief advisor, Lady Katrana Prestor, repeatedly questions the urgency of reports from places like Lakeshire, calling them exaggerations and advising against allocating royal forces. Lacking military proof, Bolvar instead deputizes independent adventurers to intervene.",["al"]={"why no stormwind army","why won't bolvar send help","lakeshire troops"},["q"]="Why won't Bolvar send soldiers to help Redridge or Westfall?"},{["a"]="Lady Katrana Prestor is the premier royal councilor to the throne of Stormwind. Bolvar respects her political acumen and deep knowledge of noble affairs. However, she continually uses her influence to counsel restraint, urging him to dismiss rumors of dragons, orcs, and Defias plots.",["al"]={"bolvar and prestor","who is lady prestor to bolvar"},["q"]="What is Bolvar's relationship with Lady Katrana Prestor?"},{["a"]="Bolvar is not related to Anduin, but he acts as the young king's fierce protector, guardian, and mentor. Bolvar stands beside Anduin's throne in Stormwind Keep, shielding the boy from court intrigue and ensuring that the Wrynn dynasty remains secure until Varian returns.",["al"]={"anduin and bolvar","is bolvar anduin's father"},["q"]="What is Bolvar's connection to young Prince Anduin?"}},["kw"]={"anduin wrynn","bolvar","fordragon","highlord","katrana prestor","regent","stormwind keep"},["n"]="Bolvar Fordragon",["s"]="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon serves as the Regent of Stormwind and Supreme Commander of its armed forces following the mysterious disappearance of King Varian Wrynn. Standing beside the young boy-king Anduin Wrynn in Stormwind Keep, he strives to hold the kingdom together amid escalating domestic turmoil. Though fiercely honorable, Bolvar often finds his martial decisions influenced and stalled by royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor.",["sec"]={{["b"]="When King Varian vanished en route to a peace summit on Theramore Isle, Stormwind was thrown into political disarray. Ten-year-old Prince Anduin was crowned to maintain continuity, but actual governing power fell to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon as Regent. Bolvar is a venerated paladin devoted to the crown, yet he faces immense strain. Stormwind's military is thinly stretched across Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood. Compounding these crises, Bolvar frequently defers to the counsel of Lady Katrana Prestor, whose dismissive advice consistently blocks him from committing royal troops to peripheral towns.",["t"]="Regent of the Realm"},{["b"]="Behind the scenes in the royal court, Bolvar's hands are tied tighter than he realizes. While town magistrates and frontier marshals beg for reinforcements against the Defias Brotherhood and Blackrock orcs, Lady Prestor subtly manipulates royal decrees and belittles all reports of danger. Bolvar respects the nobility's counsel and hesitates to move without undeniable proof, unwittingly leaving the crown paralyzed. Only when compelling evidence arrives—such as investigative warnings from Theramore or missing field officers—does the Regent bypass standard court decorum to enlist independent adventurers.",["t"]="A Web of Deceit"}}}}}
t["npc:brewmaster-drohn"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,393,32.466.0,23.509.0,24.205.0,36.200.0,44.192.0,43.188.0,36.194.0,31.141.0",["h"]="90876f",["n"]="Cebador Drohn",["s"]="Cebador Drohn. El Cebador Drohn es un maestro cervecero orco que vive colina arriba desde el bullicioso puerto de Trinquete. Tras aprender el arte de la fermentación exótica gracias a sus vínculos con el legendario pandaren errante Chen Cerveza de Trueno, Drohn elabora potentes bebidas en la árida frontera de Los Baldíos. Los aventureros que descubren barriles abandonados por todo Kalimdor a menudo acaban siendo dirigidos directamente a su porche. Con vistas a los muelles goblins de Trinquete se encuentra el Cebador Drohn, un orco que ha dedicado su oficio a la ciencia de la elaboración de cerveza en lugar del simple combate. Al frente de Destilería de Drohn desde su casa en la ladera, opera pacíficamente dentro del remanso neutral establecido por el Cártel Bonvapor de Gazlowe. Mientras que la mayoría de los orcos se conforman con grog áspero o licores sencillos, el trabajo de Drohn requiere ingredientes exóticos, equilibrios refinados de sabor y técnicas rara vez practicadas entre los suyos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Though an orc, Drohn resides under Steamwheedle protection in Ratchet; attacking him will swiftly earn the wrath of the local goblin authorities.",["profession:Cooking"]="Culinary adventurers will appreciate Drohn's precise blending of rare flora and fauna to craft world-class beverages in the middle of a desert.",["race:Orc"]="Unlike most warriors who followed Thrall to Kalimdor to build fortresses, Drohn channels the newfound peace of Durotar and the Barrens into the refined art of brewing."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Brewmaster Drohn is an orcish brewer living in Ratchet in the Barrens. He is renowned for his mastery of exotic ales and his direct ties to the brewing traditions of the wandering pandaren Chen Stormstout.",["al"]={"drohn lore","who is drohn","ratchet brewmaster"},["q"]="Who is Brewmaster Drohn?"},{["a"]="Drohn's mentor was taught how to brew Stormstout by Chen Stormstout himself, passing the knowledge down to Drohn. Later, Chen personally taught Drohn the recipe and methods required to brew Trogg Ale.",["al"]={"chen connection","how does he know chen","drohn and chen"},["q"]="How does Drohn know Chen Stormstout?"},{["a"]="Take the keg to Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet. He recognizes Chen's personal handiwork immediately and will enlist you to track down the rare indigenous ingredients needed to reproduce the brew.",["al"]={"chens empty keg","found empty keg","keg quest"},["q"]="What should I do if I find Chen's Empty Keg?"},{["a"]="Drohn is an orc, but he resides and plies his trade in the neutral goblin port of Ratchet. Attacking him ruins an Alliance adventurer's reputation with Ratchet and the Steamwheedle Cartel.",["al"]={"is drohn horde","is drohn neutral","drohn faction"},["q"]="Is Brewmaster Drohn aligned with the Horde?"},{["a"]="Through Drohn's Distillery, he crafts potent mixtures including Trogg Ale and iterations of Chen Stormstout's recipes, which require local plants and creature essences found throughout Kalimdor.",["al"]={"drohn recipes","drohns distillery brews"},["q"]="What kind of drinks does Drohn make?"},{["a"]="He can be found standing outside his house on the hill overlooking the port town of Ratchet, just northwest of the main docks in the Barrens.",["al"]={"drohn location","where is drohn","find brewmaster drohn"},["q"]="Where exactly is Drohn located?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","brewmaster","chen stormstout","distillery","drohn","ratchet","trogg ale"},["n"]="Brewmaster Drohn",["s"]="Brewmaster Drohn is an orcish brewmaster living just uphill from the bustling port of Ratchet. Having learned the art of exotic fermentation through ties connected to the legendary wandering pandaren Chen Stormstout, Drohn crafts potent beverages on the arid frontier of the Barrens. Adventurers who discover discarded kegs across Kalimdor often find themselves directed straight to his porch.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlooking the goblin docks of Ratchet sits Brewmaster Drohn, an orc who has devoted his craft to the science of brewing rather than simple combat. Running Drohn's Distillery from his hillside home, he operates peacefully within the neutral haven established by Gazlowe's Steamwheedle cartel. While most orcs settle for coarse grog or simple spirits, Drohn's work involves rare ingredients, refined balances of flavor, and techniques rarely practiced among his kin.",["t"]="A Master of the Craft in Ratchet"},{["b"]="Drohn's craft is heavily shaped by Chen Stormstout, the famed pandaren wanderer who fought alongside Rexxar and the Horde during the founding of Durotar. Drohn's mentor studied directly under Chen, learning the guarded secrets of Stormstout brews, and Chen himself later instructed Drohn in crafting Trogg Ale. When travelers stumble across Chen's distinct, discarded kegs in the wilds, Drohn is the sole local authority capable of identifying the ingredients and recreating the wanderer's potent concoctions.",["t"]="The Pandaren Connection"}}}}}
t["npc:brine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="5,239,19.431.0,32.489.0,17.313.1,13.211.0,41.204.0,42.221.0,45.229.0,31.147.0,37.178.0",["h"]="b28a57",["n"]="Salmuera",["s"]="Salmuera. Salmuera es una chamán orca que reside en las áridas colinas de Loma Espina Negra, en el sur de Los Baldíos. Como experta en los espíritus del agua, guía a los iniciados chamán por la senda espiritual para comulgar con las mareas y obtener su Tótem de agua. Encaramada a una colina azotada por el viento en el norte de Loma Espina Negra, Salmuera vive lejos de los bulliciosos puestos comerciales de Los Baldíos. A pesar de las secas sabanas que la rodean, ha dedicado su vida a comprender el elemento fluido y voluble del agua. Se indica a los chamanes de toda la Horda que busquen su sabiduría una vez que han dominado la tierra y el fuego, pues el agua requiere una paciencia y una perspectiva que pocos comprenden tan profundamente como ella.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Brine is an essential guide along your journey, testing your endurance and spirit before you can commune with water and claim your Water Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="A veteran of the wars in Hillsbrad, Brine serves the Horde not on the front lines, but by passing down the spiritual heritage of the elements to new generations."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Brine is an experienced orc shaman living isolated atop a hill in the northern part of Blackthorn Ridge in the southern Barrens. She acts as a mentor for spiritual initiates seeking communion with water spirits.",["al"]={"brine lore","who is brine","orc on blackthorn ridge"},["q"]="Who is Brine?"},{["a"]="While the Barrens are dry, water's true value and spiritual purity are often clearest where life is parched. Her solitude allows her to commune deeply with the elements away from the noise of settlements.",["al"]={"why in the barrens","why does brine live in the desert"},["q"]="Why is a water shaman living in a desert?"},{["a"]="Years ago, Brine fought alongside Horde warriors in Hillsbrad Foothills and entered Tarren Mill. There she found a small well of pure spring water, which served as a lasting symbol of life and hope amidst the ruin of war.",["al"]={"tarren mill well","brine hillsbrad","brine backstory"},["q"]="What is Brine's connection to Tarren Mill?"},{["a"]="Brine oversees several stages of the 'Call of Water' trials. She directs initiates to gather pristine water samples across the world, teaching them humility and resilience before granting the insight needed for their Water Totem.",["al"]={"brine shaman quest","how to get water totem","call of water brine"},["q"]="What role does Brine play in shaman training?"},{["a"]="She can be found sitting atop a high bluff in northern Blackthorn Ridge, located in the southern half of the Barrens, just north of Razorfen Kraul.",["al"]={"brine location","where is brine","find brine barrens"},["q"]="Where exactly is Brine located?"},{["a"]="Brine believes in finding slivers of hope and pure renewal even in times of intense pain and sorrow. She teaches that water represents life and perseverance against harsh trials.",["al"]={"brine philosophy","lessons of water"},["q"]="What philosophy guides her teachings?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","blackthorn ridge","brine","call of water","shaman","tarren mill","water totem"},["n"]="Brine",["s"]="Brine is an orc shaman residing in the arid hills of Blackthorn Ridge in the southern Barrens. As an expert on the spirits of water, she guides shaman initiates along the spiritual path to commune with the tides and earn their Water Totem.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched upon a windswept hill in northern Blackthorn Ridge, Brine lives far from the bustling trading posts of the Barrens. Despite the dry savannas surrounding her, she has dedicated her life to understanding the fluid and fickle element of water. Shaman across the Horde are directed to seek her wisdom once they have mastered earth and fire, for water requires patience and perspective that few understand as deeply as she does.",["t"]="Hermit of the Ridge"},{["b"]="In her younger years, Brine marched alongside her orc companions across the Hillsbrad Foothills, taking part in battles against human settlements. During that arduous campaign, she found herself in Tarren Mill, where she encountered a humble well fed by pure, fresh spring water. That well remained in her memory as a symbol of life persisting amidst devastation, reinforcing a lesson taught to her as a child: even in the darkest times of sorrow, a small token of hope can still be found.",["t"]="Memories of the Eastern Kingdoms"},{["b"]="Brine tests aspiring shaman by sending them on pilgrimages to gather droplets of purity from varied sources, teaching them that water can be gentle yet unyielding. Her rituals culminate in communion with the spirits of the elements, allowing shaman to bind the restorative essence of water to their totemic focus.",["t"]="The Call of Water"}}}}}
t["npc:cairne-bloodhoof"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,276,19.555.0,19.525.0,24.249.0,40.274.0,25.152.0,33.211.0",["h"]="ccb8a5",["n"]="Cairne Pezuña de Sangre",["s"]="Cairne Pezuña de Sangre. Cairne Pezuña de Sangre es el venerable gran caudillo de las tribus tauren unidas y gobernante de Cima del Trueno. Un imponente guerrero de inmensa sabiduría, unió el destino de los tauren al de la Horda de Thrall después de que los orcos ayudaran a su pueblo a escapar de la extinción a manos de los centauros. Durante generaciones, los tauren vivieron como nómadas errantes por Los Baldíos, continuamente cazados y empujados hacia la extinción por salvajes merodeadores centauros. Cuando Thrall y sus orcos llegaron a las costas de Kalimdor, Cairne reconoció en ellos una nobleza poco común. Thrall ofreció protección militar y escoltó a la desesperada caravana de Cairne a través de las llanuras hasta la seguridad de Mulgore a cambio de que los guiara hasta el Oráculo en Cima del Espolón. Al asentarse sobre las imponentes mesetas de Cima del Trueno, Cairne finalmente estableció un hogar permanente y unificado para todas las tribus tauren.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Alongside Thrall, Cairne is a founding father of the modern Horde on Kalimdor, serving as a pillar of honor, wisdom, and military power.",["race:Tauren"]="Cairne is the savior of your people, having united the scattered tribes, repelled the centaur, and led the construction of Thunder Bluff."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Cairne Bloodhoof is the High Chieftain of the united tauren tribes, chieftain of the Bloodhoof tribe, and leader of Thunder Bluff. He is an ancient warrior whose leadership and strength led the tauren out of nomadic exile and into a secure homeland.",["al"]={"who is cairne","tauren leader","high chieftain"},["q"]="Who is Cairne Bloodhoof?"},{["a"]="During the Third War, marauding centaur tribes were hunting the tauren to extinction. Thrall and his newly arrived orcs fought off the marauders and escorted Cairne's great caravan to Mulgore. In gratitude, Cairne pledged his people's loyalty and strength to Thrall's Horde.",["al"]={"why tauren join horde","cairne thrall friendship","tauren orc alliance"},["q"]="Why are the tauren allied with the orcs?"},{["a"]="He presides atop Thunder Bluff, the capital city built on the high mesas of Mulgore, ruling alongside the leaders of the various reunited tauren tribes.",["al"]={"where is cairne","cairne location","find cairne bloodhoof"},["q"]="Where does Cairne reside?"},{["a"]="Baine is Cairne's beloved son and heir. When Baine was abducted by centaur raiders, Cairne fell into deep grief, refusing to fight until Rexxar and his companions tracked Baine down and returned him safely home.",["al"]={"cairne son","is baine cairne's son","baine bloodhoof relation"},["q"]="Who is Baine Bloodhoof to Cairne?"}},["kw"]={"baine","bloodhoof","cairne","centaur","high chieftain","mulgore","thrall","thunder bluff"},["n"]="Cairne Bloodhoof",["s"]="Cairne Bloodhoof is the venerable High Chieftain of the united tauren tribes and ruler of Thunder Bluff. A towering warrior of immense wisdom, he bound the fate of the tauren to Thrall's Horde after the orcs aided his people in escaping extinction at the hands of the centaur.",["sec"]={{["b"]="For generations, the tauren lived as wandering nomads across the Barrens, continually hunted and driven toward extinction by savage centaur marauders. When Thrall and his orcs arrived on the shores of Kalimdor, Cairne recognized a rare nobility in them. Thrall offered military protection, escorting Cairne's desperate caravan across the plains to the safety of Mulgore in exchange for guidance to the Oracle at Stonetalon Peak. Settling upon the towering mesas of Thunder Bluff, Cairne finally established a permanent, unified home for all tauren tribes.",["t"]="A Nation in Mulgore"},{["b"]="Indebted to Thrall, Cairne followed the orcs to Stonetalon Peak and fought side by side with the Horde and Jaina Proudmoore's humans against the Burning Legion during the Third War. Later, when Admiral Daelin Proudmoore invaded Durotar, Cairne personally took up his ancestral runespear once more to fight alongside Rexxar after his captured son, Baine, was safely recovered. Today, Cairne stands as one of the Horde's most respected elders and Thrall's closest confidant, offering calm council against reckless warmongering.",["t"]="Pledge to the Horde"}}}}}
t["npc:calor"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="5,371,25.388.0,17.389.0,13.172.0,25.103.0,51.168.0,39.174.0,47.215.0,37.191.0",["h"]="f96395",["n"]="Calor",["s"]="Calor. Calor es un entregado habitante de Villa Oscura que ayuda a la Guardia Nocturna y a la familia Carevin a defender Bosque del Ocaso. Bajo las órdenes de Jonathan Carevin, coordina activamente los esfuerzos para dar caza a los despiadados huargen que acechan en los lúgubres bosques. Los aventureros que buscan hacer retroceder a las voraces bestias que rondan la espesura a menudo reciben sus misiones a través de él. Apostado en el asediado asentamiento de Villa Oscura, Calor colabora estrechamente con Jonathan Carevin, uno de los defensores más destacados de la villa. En medio de la penumbra constante y los terrores que acechan en Bosque del Ocaso, Calor se consagra a respaldar la misión de la casa Carevin: erradicar los horrores sobrenaturales que asedian el perímetro de la villa antes de que masacren al resto de sus habitantes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Hunters will find steady work with Calor, tracking and culling savage, otherworldly beasts that defy the natural order of the forest.",["faction:Alliance"]="Calor serves as a vital contact for Alliance champions willing to brave the gloomy woods to defend the isolated townsfolk of Darkshire."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Calor is a human allied with the Carevin family living in Darkshire. He assists in the town's defense by dispatching adventurers to hunt down dangerous threats in Duskwood.",["al"]={"calor darkshire","who is calor","calor duskwood"},["q"]="Who is Calor?"},{["a"]="Calor is stationed in Darkshire, the primary Alliance town nestled in the shadowed forests of Duskwood.",["al"]={"where is calor","calor location","calor coordinates"},["q"]="Where can Calor be found?"},{["a"]="Calor is a staunch supporter of the Carevin family. He follows the directives of Jonathan Carevin, helping him wage war against the deadly monsters plaguing the forest.",["al"]={"calor and carevin","who does calor work for","carevin family calor"},["q"]="What is Calor's relationship with Jonathan Carevin?"},{["a"]="Calor tasks adventurers with hunting the bloodthirsty worgen packs that infest the woods, particularly directing strikes against them near places such as the Rotting Orchard.",["al"]={"calor quests","what does calor want","worgen quests calor"},["q"]="What enemies does Calor have you fight?"},{["a"]="The worgen are vicious, ravenous predators that attack anything on sight. Without regular culls coordinated by figures like Calor and the Night Watch, the beasts would quickly overrun Darkshire's thin defense lines.",["al"]={"why kill worgen duskwood","duskwood worgen threat"},["q"]="Why is the worgen threat so urgent in Duskwood?"},{["a"]="While Calor works in close conjunction with town defenders and aligns with Jonathan Carevin, he primarily operates as a direct agent and supporter of the Carevin family's anti-worgen crusade.",["al"]={"calor night watch","is calor in night watch"},["q"]="Is Calor a member of the Night Watch?"}},["kw"]={"calor","carevin","darkshire","duskwood","jonathan carevin","night watch","rotting orchard","worgen"},["n"]="Calor",["s"]="Calor is a dedicated resident of Darkshire who aids the Night Watch and the Carevin family in defending Duskwood. Operating under the direction of Jonathan Carevin, he actively coordinates efforts to hunt down the vicious worgen stalking the gloomy forests. Adventurers looking to push back the ravenous beasts haunting the woods often find their assignments through him.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stationed within the beleaguered settlement of Darkshire, Calor works closely with Jonathan Carevin, one of the town's prominent defenders. Amid the endless gloom and creeping terrors of Duskwood, Calor devotes himself to supporting the Carevin household's mission: eradicating the supernatural horrors encroaching upon the town's perimeter before the remaining townsfolk are slaughtered.",["t"]="A Loyalist in the Shadows"},{["b"]="Calor's primary duty centers on confronting the feral worgen prowling the woods, particularly around blighted areas like the Rotting Orchard. These ferocious wolf-men are far more aggressive and dangerous than common beasts, slaughtering travelers and patrols alike. Calor enlists capable fighters to cull their ranks and investigate their origins, desperate to stem the bloodthirsty tide.",["t"]="The Worgen Menace"}}}}}
t["npc:captain-grayson"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,252,29.333.0,21.421.0,15.319.0,23.217.0,28.197.0,44.218.0,20.222.0,46.171.0,42.183.0",["h"]="d0b29f",["n"]="Capitán Grisillo",["s"]="Capitán Grisillo. El Capitán Grisillo es el espíritu inquieto de un capitán pirata apostado en el Faro de Poniente. Habiendo perdido su propia vida cuando su barco se estrelló contra la oscura costa, ahora vigila el faro para evitar que otros marineros sufran su mismo destino. En vida, Grisillo capitaneó un navío a lo largo de los peligrosos mares del sur de los Reinos del Este. Su viaje llegó a un violento final frente a los escarpados bajíos de Páramos de Poniente, en una noche en que el fuego del faro se había apagado. Arrojado contra las rocas, Grisillo pereció junto a su barco, solo para despertar como un fantasma atado al mundo terrenal, atrapado en la costa.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Though Grayson is an undead spirit, his purpose is selfless and protective. Assisting him honors the sacred duty of defending the helpless and purging the murderous tides of murlocs.",["class:Priest"]="Grayson's spirit is anchored by guilt and grief over watching an innocent family die. Offering aid brings a measure of solace to his restless soul.",["faction:Alliance"]="With the Defias Brotherhood choking Westfall and Stormwind neglecting its borders, it falls to visiting Alliance travelers to answer Grayson's plea and secure the lighthouse flame."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Captain Grayson is a human ghost pirate residing at the Westfall Lighthouse. After wrecking on the coast because the beacon went out, his spirit took it upon himself to maintain the light and protect passing mariners.",["al"]={"grayson identity","who is the ghost pirate","lighthouse ghost"},["q"]="Who is Captain Grayson?"},{["a"]="He died when his pirate vessel was driven onto the treacherous rocks along Westfall's shore. The lighthouse was dark that night, giving him and his crew no warning before their ship was torn apart.",["al"]={"grayson death","how did grayson become a ghost","what killed captain grayson"},["q"]="How did Captain Grayson die?"},{["a"]="The keeper and his family were attacked by coastal murlocs. Though they escaped the initial assault and returned to relight the beacon, Old Murk-Eye rallied a second raid and slaughtered them all before Grayson's eyes.",["al"]={"where is the lighthouse keeper","what happened to the keepers","lighthouse family"},["q"]="What happened to the real lighthouse keeper?"},{["a"]="Old Murk-Eye is a cunning and vicious murloc chieftain stalking the Westfall shoreline. He led the assault that killed the lighthouse keeper's family and poses a constant threat to anyone attempting to keep the beacon lit.",["al"]={"murk eye lore","old murk eye","murloc leader westfall"},["q"]="Who is Old Murk-Eye?"},{["a"]="Having drowned because the coastline was pitch black, Grayson considers it his solemn duty in the afterlife to ensure no other sailors meet that same fate upon the shoals.",["al"]={"grayson motivation","why light the beacon"},["q"]="Why does Grayson want the lighthouse kept lit?"},{["a"]="No. Despite his pirate background in life, Grayson harbors no ill will toward the living. He has witnessed too much slaughter and seeks only peace and assistance in tending the flame.",["al"]={"is grayson friendly","grayson hostile"},["q"]="Is Captain Grayson hostile to adventurers?"}},["kw"]={"captain grayson","ghost pirate","grayson","lighthouse","old murk-eye","westfall","westfall lighthouse"},["n"]="Captain Grayson",["s"]="Captain Grayson is the restless spirit of a pirate captain stationed at the Westfall Lighthouse. Having lost his own life when his ship smashed against the dark coastline, he now watches over the beacon to prevent other sailors from suffering his fate.",["sec"]={{["b"]="In life, Grayson captained a vessel along the perilous southern seas of the Eastern Kingdoms. His voyage came to a violent end off the jagged shoals of Westfall on a night when the lighthouse fire had gone dark. Cast upon the rocks, Grayson perished alongside his ship, only to awaken as an earthbound phantom trapped upon the coast.",["t"]="A Life Cut Short by the Rocks"},{["b"]="Drawn to the Westfall Lighthouse in death, Grayson hoped to find answers about the afterlife. Instead, he witnessed sheer tragedy. A notorious murloc known as Old Murk-Eye drove the lighthouse keeper and his family away. Though the keepers bravely returned to rekindle the flame, Old Murk-Eye rallied the surrounding murlocs for a second, brutal slaughter. Grayson could only watch helplessly as the family was butchered.",["t"]="Tragedy at the Beacon"},{["b"]="With the keepers dead and Westfall crumbling under neglect, Captain Grayson took the solemn burden of the beacon upon his spectral shoulders. He seeks aid from passing adventurers to gather fuel for the great flame and avenge the slaughtered family by hunting down Old Murk-Eye and driving back the coastal murloc tide.",["t"]="A Ghostly Vigil"}}}}}
t["npc:captain-greenskin"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,320,24.355.0,15.338.0,25.178.0,56.174.0,35.159.0,45.173.0,37.134.0,67.144.0",["h"]="54c149",["n"]="Capitán Verdetez",["s"]="Capitán Verdetez. El Capitán Verdetez es un pirata goblin de élite que supervisa la construcción y la tripulación del colosal acorazado de Edwin VanCleef. Oculto en las profundidades de la ensenada subterránea de Las Minas de la Muerte, comanda las fuerzas piratas contratadas por la Hermandad Defias. Su objetivo es tener el buque de guerra listo para zarpar contra Ventormenta. El Capitán Verdetez, que patrulla la cubierta principal del gigantesco acorazado en construcción en la ensenada de Las Minas de la Muerte, representa la columna vertebral naval de la conspiración de los Defias. Verdetez, un avezado marinero goblin que operaba anteriormente desde Bahía del Botín, fue incorporado al círculo íntimo de Edwin VanCleef para transformar una caverna subterránea en un dique seco destinado a una máquina de guerra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Greenskin stands at the apex of Defias piracy, heavily guarded by corsairs and brutes right on the warship's deck.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces, Captain Greenskin represents the maritime threat of the Defias rebellion; if his juggernaut breaches the coast, the undefended shores of Westfall and Stormwind are at direct risk."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Captain Greenskin is a goblin pirate captain hired by Edwin VanCleef to supervise the completion and operation of the Defias Brotherhood's secret war juggernaut in the Deadmines.",["al"]={"greenskin lore","who is greenskin","captain greenskin"},["q"]="Who is Captain Greenskin?"},{["a"]="Greenskin originally hails from Booty Bay in the southern reaches of Stranglethorn Vale, where he formerly commanded a fleet of pirate vessels before entering VanCleef's pay.",["al"]={"greenskin origin","where is greenskin from","greenskin booty bay"},["q"]="Where did Greenskin come from before joining the Defias?"},{["a"]="His command includes his first mate, the tauren Mr. Smite, as well as Cookie the murloc cook and a contingent of Defias pirates patrolling the ironclad's deck.",["al"]={"greenskin crew","first mate","greenskin minions"},["q"]="Who serves under Captain Greenskin?"},{["a"]="He is tasked with making the massive ironclad warship seaworthy and prepared to sail out of the subterranean grotto into the Great Sea to strike at the kingdom of Stormwind.",["al"]={"what does greenskin do","why is greenskin here"},["q"]="What is Greenskin's purpose in the Deadmines?"},{["a"]="He paces the main deck of the large juggernaut anchored in the final cavern of the Deadmines, guarding the approach to Edwin VanCleef.",["al"]={"greenskin location","where is captain greenskin"},["q"]="Where can Captain Greenskin be found?"},{["a"]="He is a mercenary pirate captain in the direct employ of Edwin VanCleef, commanding the naval forces aligned with the Defias Brotherhood's plot.",["al"]={"is greenskin defias","greenskin faction"},["q"]="Is Captain Greenskin part of the Defias Brotherhood or a mercenary?"}},["kw"]={"booty bay","captain greenskin","deadmines","goblin pirate","greenskin","juggernaut","smite","vancleef"},["n"]="Captain Greenskin",["s"]="Captain Greenskin is an elite goblin pirate overseeing the construction and crew of Edwin VanCleef's massive ironclad juggernaut. Hidden deep in the subterranean cove of the Deadmines, he commands the pirate forces hired by the Defias Brotherhood. His goal is to bring the warship to readiness to sail against Stormwind.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Pacing the main deck of the gigantic juggernaut under construction in the Deadmines cove, Captain Greenskin represents the naval backbone of the Defias conspiracy. A seasoned goblin mariner who previously operated out of Booty Bay, Greenskin was brought into Edwin VanCleef's inner circle to turn an underground cavern into a drydock for an engine of war.",["t"]="Master of the Juggernaut"},{["b"]="Greenskin does not command an ordinary crew of stonemasons or bandits. Under his direct watch serve seasoned cutthroats, including his fearsome tauren first mate Mr. Smite and the murloc ship's cook, Cookie. Together, they hold the ship's gangplanks and upper deck, standing between intruders and VanCleef's private cabin atop the bridge.",["t"]="A Pirate's Crew"}}}}}
t["npc:captain-stoutfist"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,302,20.437.0,20.430.0,20.439.1,25.214.0,35.99.0,45.257.0,29.215.0,58.263.0,44.205.0",["h"]="aa82a2",["n"]="Capitán Puñorrecio",["s"]="Capitán Puñorrecio. El Capitán Puñorrecio es el oficial enano al mando de las defensas militares en el Puerto de Menethil, en Los Humedales. Con el clan Faucedraco avanzando agresivamente desde sus fortalezas pantanosas, Puñorrecio coordina maniobras defensivas y contraofensivas para garantizar que este vital puerto de la Alianza no caiga. El Puerto de Menethil sirve como el principal puerto de aguas profundas que conecta Forjaz y Ventormenta con las tierras bajas pantanosas de Los Humedales y el mar más allá. Como oficial al mando de la localidad, el Capitán Puñorrecio soporta la pesada carga de mantener sus muelles, la población civil y la guarnición a salvo de las amenazas circundantes. Los pantanales son notoriamente peligrosos, pero el mayor peligro para el asentamiento es una oleada organizada de orcos renegados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="A no-nonsense dwarven tactician, Stoutfist values bold martial strikes over cautious fortification, putting warriors on the front line to dismantle enemy artillery and leadership.",["faction:Alliance"]="Captain Stoutfist holds the line at one of the Alliance's most crucial maritime hubs, keeping naval routes open between Khaz Modan, Stormwind, and distant outposts.",["race:Dwarf"]="Stoutfist represents the rugged resolve of Ironforge's military, entrusted with safeguarding vital lowlands infrastructure far below the safety of the mountain peaks."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Captain Stoutfist is the dwarf military commander tasked with defending Menethil Harbor. He coordinates garrison defenses, assesses regional threats, and recruits volunteers to push back enemies targeting the port.",["al"]={"captain stoutfist","stoutfist menethil","menethil captain"},["q"]="Who is Captain Stoutfist?"},{["a"]="He is stationed inside Menethil Harbor, the main Alliance hub on the western coast of the Wetlands.",["al"]={"stoutfist location","where is captain stoutfist","find stoutfist"},["q"]="Where is Captain Stoutfist located?"},{["a"]="The local garrison is stretched thin across the Wetlands. With Dragonmaw orcs seizing the mountain passes at Dun Algaz and encroaching on the town, Stoutfist lacks the regular manpower to launch offensive strikes and maintain harbor security simultaneously.",["al"]={"why stoutfist need help","menethil defense problems"},["q"]="Why does Captain Stoutfist need outside help?"},{["a"]="Nek'rosh Skullcrusher is the ruthless leader of the Dragonmaw orcs operating in the Wetlands. Captain Stoutfist orders his death to shatter the orcs' coordination and protect Menethil Harbor from an all-out assault.",["al"]={"who is nekrosh","nekrosh skullcrusher","dragonmaw boss wetlands"},["q"]="Who is Nek'rosh Skullcrusher?"},{["a"]="Dun Algaz is the vital mountain pass connecting Loch Modan and Ironforge to the Wetlands. When Dragonmaw orcs pushed into the pass, Mountaineer Valstag Ironjaw warned that Menethil was endangered, redirecting adventurers to Stoutfist to help reinforce the harbor.",["al"]={"dun algaz stoutfist","algaz gauntlet connection"},["q"]="How does Dun Algaz connect to Captain Stoutfist's mission?"},{["a"]="The Dragonmaw assembled siege weaponry to batter down fortifications and siege Menethil Harbor directly. Stoutfist directs champions to sabotage these catapults before they can be rolled into firing range.",["al"]={"nekroshs gambit catapults","dragonmaw catapults"},["q"]="What threat do the Dragonmaw catapults pose?"}},["kw"]={"captain stoutfist","dragonmaw","dun algaz","dwarf","ironforge","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","wetlands"},["n"]="Captain Stoutfist",["s"]="Captain Stoutfist is the dwarven officer in charge of military defenses at Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. With the Dragonmaw clan pushing aggressively out of their marshland strongholds, Stoutfist coordinates defensive maneuvers and counter-offensives to ensure the vital Alliance port does not fall.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Menethil Harbor serves as the principal deepwater port connecting Ironforge and Stormwind to the marshy lowlands of the Wetlands and the sea beyond. As the town's commanding officer, Captain Stoutfist bears the heavy burden of keeping its docks, civilian populace, and garrison secure against surrounding threats. The marshlands are notoriously hazardous, but the biggest peril to the settlement is an organized surge from renegade orcs.",["t"]="Defender of Menethil"},{["b"]="The Dragonmaw clan, entrenched within the Wetlands since the Second War, has begun pushing their operations directly toward the roadways and passes. By infiltrating Dun Algaz, they threaten to sever the overland lifeline connecting Loch Modan and Ironforge to Menethil Harbor. Facing a severe shortage of troops, Captain Stoutfist relies on visiting Alliance volunteers recommended by Mountaineer Valstag Ironjaw to stem the tide.",["t"]="The Dragonmaw Threat"},{["b"]="Rather than waiting for a siege, Captain Stoutfist spearheads a aggressive campaign against the orc encampments. He directs allied forces to seize war banners near Whelgar's Excavation Site, sabotage Dragonmaw catapults preparing for an assault, and eliminate the clan's ruthless local chieftain, Nek'rosh Skullcrusher. By cutting down Nek'rosh, Stoutfist aims to break the spine of the orc offensive before Menethil Harbor is overwhelmed.",["t"]="Striking at Nek'rosh"}}}}}
t["npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="29,357,17.405.0,23.461.1,37.139.0,47.148.0,29.186.0,41.147.0,32.93.0,49.150.0",["h"]="7aa3d7",["n"]="Ingeniero Jefe Hinderweir VII",["s"]="Ingeniero Jefe Hinderweir VII. El Ingeniero Jefe Hinderweir VII es un veterano ingeniero enano apostado en lo alto de la Presa de las Tres Cabezas, en Loch Modan. Con la tarea de mantener y defender esta monumental hazaña de ingeniería, supervisa sus delicados mecanismos mientras vigila posibles sabotajes. Quienes hablan con él descubren rápidamente que graves peligros amenazan la integridad de la gran presa. La Presa de las Tres Cabezas es uno de los mayores logros de la cantería e ingeniería enanas, conteniendo las inmensas aguas de Loch Modan. El Ingeniero Jefe Hinderweir VII carga con la inmensa responsabilidad de mantener su estructura y su maquinaria operativa. Situado a lo largo de la cresta de la presa, vigila los canales fluviales, las compuertas y los puntos de tensión estructural frente a los elementos y los peligros locales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance cannot afford to let the dam fall; catastrophic failure would disrupt supply routes and devastate allied lands north of Loch Modan.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the sheer mechanical scale of Hinderweir's charge, as the Stonewrought Dam represents a peerless mix of civil architecture and mechanical control.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Hinderweir represents the solemn duty of preserving Khaz Modan's greatest stonecraft achievements against outside malice."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is the dwarven supervisor in charge of maintaining and defending the Stonewrought Dam in northern Loch Modan.",["al"]={"hinderweir","chief engineer","dam engineer"},["q"]="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?"},{["a"]="He can be found standing along the top walkway of the Stonewrought Dam, which spans the northern edge of Loch Modan near the border to the Wetlands.",["al"]={"hinderweir location","where is hinderweir","find hinderweir"},["q"]="Where can I find Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?"},{["a"]="The Stonewrought Dam is a massive dwarven architectural wonder that holds back the waters of Loch Modan, preventing the lake from violently spilling into the lower wetlands to the north.",["al"]={"what is the dam","stonewrought dam purpose","why is the dam important"},["q"]="What is the Stonewrought Dam?"},{["a"]="Hinderweir investigates active sabotage against the dam, discovering evidence of dark plots and explosive devices planted to crack its foundations.",["al"]={"dam threats","a dark threat looms","who wants to destroy the dam"},["q"]="What threats is Hinderweir worried about?"},{["a"]="VII is the Roman numeral for seven. The reason it appears in Hinderweir's name is unrecorded.",["al"]={"hinderweir name","why the seventh","hinderweir vii meaning"},["q"]="Why does his name include 'VII'?"},{["a"]="He offers the quest chain 'A Dark Threat Looms', which directs adventurers to investigate tampering and protect the Stonewrought Dam from destruction.",["al"]={"hinderweir quests","quests at the dam","a dark threat looms quest"},["q"]="What quests does Chief Engineer Hinderweir offer?"}},["kw"]={"a dark threat looms","dwarf","engineer","hinderweir","loch modan","sabotage","stonewrought dam"},["n"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",["s"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII is a veteran dwarven engineer stationed atop the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan. Tasked with the upkeep and defense of this monumental feat of engineering, he oversees its delicate mechanisms while keeping watch for sabotage. Those who speak with him quickly discover that grave dangers threaten the integrity of the great dam.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Stonewrought Dam is one of the crowning achievements of dwarven stonecraft and engineering, holding back the massive waters of the Loch. Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII bears the immense responsibility of maintaining its structure and operational machinery. Perched along the crest of the dam, he monitors the waterways, sluice gates, and structural stress points against the elements and local hazards.",["t"]="Master of the Dam"},{["b"]="Running the dam is more than routine maintenance; dark forces continually test its defenses. Hinderweir uncovers signs of calculated sabotage orchestrated by hostile elements in the region. Aware that a catastrophic breach would flood the lowlands and devastate Khaz Modan's delicate infrastructure, the Chief Engineer enlists reliable Alliance adventurers to trace the conspiracy, disarm hidden explosives, and neutralize the threat before the stone gives way.",["t"]="Sabotage and Subversion"}}}}}
t["npc:chief-hawkwind"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,371,21.430.0,17.420.0,22.380.0,22.222.0,38.252.0,51.241.0,35.227.0,48.247.0,50.151.0",["h"]="aaccd3",["n"]="Jefe Vientaguilar",["s"]="Jefe Vientaguilar. El Jefe Vientaguilar es el líder tribal del Campamento Narache, el terreno de pruebas enclavado en la Mesa de la Nube Roja de Mulgore. Responsable de guiar a la juventud de los Shu'halo, tutela a los nuevos aventureros mientras se embarcan en sus tradicionales ritos de iniciación. Bajo su atenta mirada, los jóvenes valientes aprenden humildad, respeto por la tierra y la fuerza necesaria para proteger a su pueblo. Erguido en el corazón del Campamento Narache, el Jefe Vientaguilar carga con la solemne responsabilidad de preparar a la próxima generación de tauren para el resto del mundo. La Mesa de la Nube Roja sirve como un refugio protegido donde los noveles cazadores, chamanes, druidas y guerreros emprenden los ancestrales Ritos de la Madre Tierra. Vientaguilar supervisa estas costumbres, asegurándose de que cada joven aprenda el deber y la resistencia antes de aventurarse más allá de la seguridad de la mesa.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Hawkwind's teachings ensure that newly raised tauren braves step forward not just as capable warriors and spellcasters, but as steadfast and honorable allies to the young Horde.",["race:Tauren"]="As the first chieftain to guide you on your journey, Chief Hawkwind instills the foundational values of the Shu'halo: reverence for the Earthmother, loyalty to the tribe, and humility in strength."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Chief Hawkwind is the chieftain of Camp Narache in the Red Cloud Mesa. He oversees tribal matters in the area and mentors young tauren as they prepare to take their first steps into the wider world of Mulgore and Kalimdor.",["al"]={"hawkwind","chief hawkwind lore","who is the chief at camp narache"},["q"]="Who is Chief Hawkwind?"},{["a"]="The Rites of the Earthmother are a traditional series of sacred trials undertaken by young tauren coming of age. Guided by elders like Chief Hawkwind, these rites test humility, strength, courage, and spiritual connection to the land and the ancestors.",["al"]={"tauren rites","rites of earthmother","what are the rites"},["q"]="What are the Rites of the Earthmother?"},{["a"]="Hawkwind assigns 'A Humble Task' to remind young braves that service and respect for the community are as vital as martial strength. Gathering fresh water for tribal elders teaches patience and humility before initiates are sent into battle.",["al"]={"a humble task","why fetch water","hawkwind water quest"},["q"]="Why does Chief Hawkwind have you fetch water first?"},{["a"]="Camp Narache is under constant pressure from hostile Bristleback quilboar who inhabit the surrounding hills of Red Cloud Mesa. Chief Hawkwind must organize the defense of the mesa and send initiates to thin the quillboar ranks.",["al"]={"narache threats","who is attacking camp narache","quilboar camp narache"},["q"]="What threat is Camp Narache facing?"},{["a"]="Once a young brave completes the preliminary rites on the mesa, Chief Hawkwind directs them down into the sprawling valleys of Mulgore, sending them toward Bloodhoof Village to continue their trials under the guidance of Cairne Bloodhoof's elders.",["al"]={"where do i go after hawkwind","after camp narache","leaving red cloud mesa"},["q"]="Where does Chief Hawkwind send adventurers next?"},{["a"]="Yes, Greatmother Hawkwind is his mother. The Hawkwind family has long held deep roots and leadership roles among the tauren dwelling on Red Cloud Mesa.",["al"]={"greatmother hawkwind relation","hawkwind family","who is greatmother hawkwind"},["q"]="Is Chief Hawkwind related to Greatmother Hawkwind?"}},["kw"]={"a humble task","bristleback","camp narache","chief hawkwind","mulgore","red cloud mesa","rite of strength","rites of the earthmother","tauren chieftain"},["n"]="Chief Hawkwind",["s"]="Chief Hawkwind is the tribal leader of Camp Narache, the proving grounds nestled in the Red Cloud Mesa of Mulgore. Responsible for guiding the youth of the Shu'halo, he mentors new adventurers as they embark on their traditional rites of passage. Under his watchful gaze, young braves learn humility, respect for the land, and the strength needed to protect their people.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing at the heart of Camp Narache, Chief Hawkwind carries the solemn responsibility of preparing the next generation of tauren for the wider world. Red Cloud Mesa serves as a sheltered haven where fledgling hunters, shamans, druids, and warriors undertake the ancient Rites of the Earthmother. Hawkwind oversees these customs, ensuring that every youth learns duty and endurance before venturing beyond the safety of the mesa.",["t"]="Chieftain of the Mesa"},{["b"]="Hawkwind's lessons begin with humility rather than martial glory. He sends initiates on simple chores, such as fetching clean spring water, to instill reverence for the natural world and their elders. Only after demonstrating a humble heart are braves guided toward tests of martial prowess, culminating in trials that test their resolve against the aggressive Bristleback quilboar encroaching upon the ancestral plains.",["t"]="Guiding the Rites"},{["b"]="Beyond his role as a mentor, Chief Hawkwind must reckon with rising dangers right at his camp's doorstep. The Bristleback tribe has grown increasingly bold, pressing hard against the perimeter of Red Cloud Mesa. Hawkwind coordinates the defense of the settlement, tasking newly proven braves with blunting the quilboar assaults to ensure the sacred training grounds remain secure.",["t"]="Defending Camp Narache"}}}}}
t["npc:clerk-daltry"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,263,18.441.0,15.465.0,21.414.1,30.199.0,40.224.0,31.267.0,58.232.0,43.172.0,42.158.0",["h"]="98aed4",["n"]="Dependiente Daltry",["s"]="Dependiente Daltry. El Dependiente Daltry es el encargado del registro civil destinado en ayuntamiento de Villa Oscura, en Bosque del Ocaso. Rodeado de libros de contabilidad y registros, ayuda a investigar el pasado de la villa y a localizar documentos históricos, aunque sus archivos estén algo descuidados y desactualizados. Mientras Villa Oscura lucha contra las bestias que la acechan, horrores no-muertos y una penumbra sobrenatural, los quehaceres cívicos cotidianos recaen en el Dependiente Daltry. Trabajando en el ayuntamiento de Villa Oscura junto a Lord Ello Cerranegro y el consejo local, Daltry mantiene los libros de cuentas históricos, los censos de propiedades y los datos del padrón de la villa. En una región fracturada por el desastre, sus registros figuran entre los pocos vínculos supervivientes con los días anteriores a que Grand Hamlet cayera en la sombra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance investigators uncovering the sinister mysteries of Duskwood, Clerk Daltry is an essential bureaucratic contact for long-lost records and cold case files.",["race:Human"]="Daltry preserves what remains of the historical heritage of Grand Hamlet before the darkness descended upon the woodland realm."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Clerk Daltry is found inside the Darkshire Town Hall, located in the central village of Darkshire in Duskwood. He stands amidst the town officials and council members, managing the municipal records.",["al"]={"clerk daltry location","where is daltry","darkshire clerk location"},["q"]="Where is Clerk Daltry located?"},{["a"]="He serves as Darkshire's civic clerk, tasked with preserving documents, town rolls, and legal registries. He assists adventurers who need archival information regarding former residents, land claims, or historical inquiries.",["al"]={"what does daltry do","daltry role","who is clerk daltry"},["q"]="What is Clerk Daltry's job in Darkshire?"},{["a"]="Duskwood has suffered years of isolation, magical corruption, and violent turmoil. With the town's focus consumed by immediate survival against the Night Watch's enemies, maintaining up-to-date ledgers has often fallen by the wayside, leaving his archives fragmented.",["al"]={"why are daltry's records bad","outdated records duskwood","missing ledgers daltry"},["q"]="Why are his records incomplete?"},{["a"]="Daltry is a crucial figure in 'The Legend of Stalvan' storyline, helping players track down the elusive past of Stalvan Mistmantle. He also assists with investigations such as 'The Carevin Family' and 'The Shadowy Search Continues'.",["al"]={"daltry quests","what quests from daltry","clerk daltry quest chain"},["q"]="What questlines does Clerk Daltry start or participate in?"},{["a"]="It is widely suspected they share family ties given their common surname and service roles, though Clerk Daltry stays strictly focused on his municipal duties in Darkshire.",["al"]={"surveyor daltry relation","daltry family"},["q"]="Is Clerk Daltry related to Surveyor Daltry?"},{["a"]="No. Clerk Daltry is an Alliance-affiliated municipal servant. Darkshire and its town hall are guarded by the Night Watch and hostile to all Horde adventurers.",["al"]={"is daltry friendly to horde","can horde talk to daltry"},["q"]="Can Horde players speak with Clerk Daltry?"}},["kw"]={"carevin","clerk daltry","darkshire","duskwood","ledgers","mistmantle","records","stalvan","town hall"},["n"]="Clerk Daltry",["s"]="Clerk Daltry is the civic record keeper stationed in Darkshire Town Hall in Duskwood. Surrounded by ledgers and registry books, he helps investigate the village's past and track down historical records, even if his archives are somewhat neglected and out of date.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Darkshire struggles against encroaching beasts, undead horrors, and supernatural gloom, everyday civic duties fall to Clerk Daltry. Working out of the Darkshire Town Hall alongside Lord Ello Ebonlocke and the local council, Daltry maintains the town's historical ledgers, property rolls, and census data. In a region fractured by disaster, his records are among the few surviving links to the days before Grand Hamlet fell into shadow.",["t"]="Town Record Keeper"},{["b"]="Because Darkshire has been cut off from regular Stormwind administration, Daltry's record-keeping is notoriously imperfect. Old documents go missing, ledgers fall behind, and vital town files are frequently misplaced or damaged. Adventurers investigating local cold cases or long-lost residents frequently consult him, only to find that uncovering the truth requires digging through overlooked notes or venturing out into the dangerous woods to recover lost papers.",["t"]="The Paper Trail"},{["b"]="Daltry plays a central role in untangling the dark mystery of Stalvan Mistmantle. When an ominous family legend leads investigators back to Darkshire, Daltry searches his archives for records of the former schoolteacher. Because his town registry entries on Stalvan are fragmented, Daltry must send seekers across town and into forgotten homesteads across the kingdom to piece together the tragic and bloody truth.",["t"]="The Legend of Stalvan"}}}}}
t["npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="21,279,21.405.0,40.498.1,29.201.0,39.158.0,44.213.0,44.218.0,54.162.0,43.174.0",["h"]="196ac5",["n"]="Vigiarrisco Cuernolargo",["s"]="Vigiarrisco Cuernolargo. El Vigiarrisco Cuernolargo es el estoico líder tauren apostado en lo alto de Poblado Viento Libre, en Las Mil Agujas. Con la tarea de salvaguardar el aislado puesto de avanzada de la Horda, coordina las defensas contra los invasores centauros Galak y vigila las sospechosas maquinaciones de la tribu Tótem Siniestro. Encaramado sobre las imponentes agujas de roca de Las Mil Agujas, Poblado Viento Libre depende de ojos avizores y un liderazgo firme para sobrevivir. El Vigiarrisco Cuernolargo supervisa la seguridad diaria de este precario asentamiento. Con fuerzas hostiles congregándose en el fondo del cañón y a lo largo de las crestas vecinas, Cuernolargo actúa como el principal coordinador del asentamiento para los informes de exploración y las labores defensivas militares.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post is the vital link securing supply lines across southern Kalimdor, and Longhorn ensures the Horde retains its precarious foothold amidst hostile centaur territory.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, Longhorn represents the frontier spirit of the Shu'halo, keeping watch over contested sacred mesas while navigating the bitter, unresolved friction with the Grimtotem tribe."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Cliffwatcher Longhorn is the tauren authority figure in command of Freewind Post, the Horde's towering outpost in Thousand Needles. He organizes scouts, defense patrols, and responses to local threats.",["al"]={"cliffwatcher longhorn info","who is longhorn","freewind post leader"},["q"]="Who is Cliffwatcher Longhorn?"},{["a"]="He is located atop the main mesa of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, accessible by taking the lift up from the canyon floor and crossing the wooden bridges.",["al"]={"cliffwatcher longhorn location","where is longhorn"},["q"]="Where can I find Cliffwatcher Longhorn?"},{["a"]="Reports brought in by scouts like Brave Moonhorn show an alarming surge in Galak centaur hostility. Longhorn orders proactive strikes to pacify the clan and prevent them from overwhelming the outpost's approaches.",["al"]={"why kill centaur","pacify the centaur lore","centaur threat thousand needles"},["q"]="Why is Longhorn concerned about the centaur?"},{["a"]="While technically living among the Horde, the Grimtotem clan behaves with open secrecy and malice. Longhorn suspects foul play and commissions adventurers to steal their hidden notes to discover what they are plotting.",["al"]={"longhorn grimtotem","grimtotem spying reason"},["q"]="What is his interest in the Grimtotem tribe?"},{["a"]="Arnak Grimtotem carried out a violent attack against the post's inhabitants. Longhorn issues a bounty on his head to ensure Arnak faces justice for his treachery.",["al"]={"wanted arnak grimtotem","arnak bounty lore"},["q"]="Who is Arnak Grimtotem and why does Longhorn want him?"},{["a"]="Yes, his brother Nataka Longhorn is stationed far to the west at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace. Preoccupied with duty, Cliffwatcher rarely finds the opportunity to write him.",["al"]={"longhorn brother","nataka longhorn brother"},["q"]="Does Cliffwatcher Longhorn have any family?"}},["kw"]={"arnak grimtotem","brave moonhorn","cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","galak","grimtotem","nataka longhorn","thousand needles"},["n"]="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",["s"]="Cliffwatcher Longhorn is the stoic tauren leader stationed high atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Tasked with safeguarding the isolated Horde outpost, he coordinates defenses against encroaching Galak centaur and monitors the suspicious machinations of the Grimtotem tribe.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched upon the soaring rock spires of Thousand Needles, Freewind Post relies on sharp eyes and steady leadership to survive. Cliffwatcher Longhorn oversees the day-to-day security of this precarious settlement. With hostile forces gathering on the canyon floor below and along neighboring ridges, Longhorn acts as the settlement's primary coordinator for scouting reports and defensive military efforts.",["t"]="Guardian of the Mesas"},{["b"]="Longhorn contends with threats on multiple fronts. Down in the canyon, the aggressive Galak centaur relentlessly probe the perimeter, prompting him to dispatch adventurers to push them back and curb their numbers. Even more troubling to him, however, are the Grimtotem tauren. Deeply distrustful of their secretive camp near the post, Longhorn arranges reconnaissance to seize their hidden notes, uncovering troubling evidence of internal treachery, including the violent crimes of Arnak Grimtotem.",["t"]="Centaur Hostility and Grimtotem Intrigue"}}}}}
t["npc:coleman-farthing"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,371,16.546.0,24.507.0,36.109.0,49.315.0,35.254.0,44.239.0,51.293.0,47.134.0",["h"]="197399",["n"]="Coleman Lontananza",["s"]="Coleman Lontananza. Coleman Lontananza es un amargado superviviente Renegado que reside en el Mesón La Horca en Rémol. En vida, trabajó para la acaudalada dinastía Agamand en sus extensos molinos de harina en el norte de Tirisfal. Convencido para quedarse y defender la finca contra la Plaga, murió junto a sus compañeros de trabajo y ahora dedica su no-muerte a cobrarse venganza de sus antiguos amos. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, Coleman Lontananza se ganaba honradamente la vida como obrero en los Molinos de Agamand, la mayor explotación agrícola y harinera de los Claros de Tirisfal. Cuando la Plaga arrasó Lordaeron, la aristocrática familia Agamand se negó a huir de sus valiosas tierras. En su lugar, instaron a sus sirvientes y peones a tomar las armas junto a ellos, prometiendo que podrían defender las granjas contra la horda de no-muertos. Coleman y sus compañeros se quedaron, confiando en sus señores, una decisión que les costó la vida a todos y cada uno de ellos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Coleman points aspiring warriors directly toward the Agamand Family Crypt, urging them to plunder the martial heirlooms of a fallen aristocratic house to arm themselves for the wars ahead.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Coleman represents the shared resentment many commoners hold toward Lordaeron's old nobility, whose arrogance and pride often hastened their subjects' demise during the plague."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Coleman Farthing spends his days inside the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, located in central Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"coleman farthing location","where is coleman farthing","coleman farthing brill"},["q"]="Where can Coleman Farthing be found?"},{["a"]="When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, the Agamand patriarchs convinced their workers—including Coleman—to stay and fight to protect the mills rather than flee to safety. The entire workforce was slaughtered as a result. Coleman views their rallying cry as arrogant manipulation that led him directly to his death.",["al"]={"why does coleman hate agamands","coleman farthing motivation","agamand mills grudge"},["q"]="Why does Coleman hate the Agamand family so much?"},{["a"]="The sprawling estate was completely overrun by the Scourge. Its wind-driven mills stand ruined and haunted, while the Agamand family members and their slaughtered workers wander the blighted fields as mindlessly hostile undead under the Lich King's sway.",["al"]={"what happened to agamand mills","agamand mills lore","who owns agamand mills"},["q"]="What happened to the Agamand Mills?"},{["a"]="Coleman directs adventurers to journey north to the Agamand Mills to cull the roaming undead, slay the risen members of the Agamand lineage to recover their remains for desecration, and raid the Agamand Family Crypt for ancestral weaponry.",["al"]={"coleman farthing quests","agamand quests brill"},["q"]="What tasks does Coleman give to adventurers?"},{["a"]="Coleman sees the Agamands' ancestral weaponry as symbols of the hollow pride that led his fellow workers to their deaths. He sends skilled warriors to plunder these relics from the family crypt, both to strip the dynasty of its honor and put the weapons to practical use against their enemies.",["al"]={"agamand heirlooms quest lore","why steal agamand weapons"},["q"]="Why does Coleman want the Agamand heirloom weapons?"},{["a"]="They share a surname and origins in the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, but there is no confirmed record of their specific familial ties.",["al"]={"bishop farthing relation","coleman farthing family"},["q"]="Is Coleman Farthing related to Bishop Farthing?"}},["kw"]={"agamand heirlooms","agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","deaths in the family","gallows' end tavern","lordaeron","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Coleman Farthing",["s"]="Coleman Farthing is a bitter Forsaken survivor residing in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. In life, he worked for the wealthy Agamand dynasty at their extensive flour mills in northern Tirisfal. Convinced to stay and defend the estate against the Scourge, he died alongside his fellow laborers, and now dedicates his undeath to exacting vengeance on his former masters.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, Coleman Farthing earned an honest living as a laborer at the Agamand Mills, the largest milling and agricultural operation in Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge poured across Lordaeron, the aristocratic Agamand family refused to flee their valuable lands. Instead, they urged their household and laborers to take up arms alongside them, promising they could hold the farmsteads against the undead horde. Coleman and his fellow workers stayed, believing their masters—a decision that cost every last one of them their lives.",["t"]="A Bitter Servant"},{["b"]="Raised into undeath only to break free under the banner of the Forsaken, Coleman harbors a burning hatred for the Agamands. Rather than blaming only the Scourge, he blames the sheer hubris and greed of his employers for tricking their staff into an impossible last stand. Now loitering in Brill's tavern, Coleman enlists Horde champions to march into the blighted mills, cut down the risen Agamand kin, and shatter the heirloom relics housed within their family crypt so that their legacy is utterly erased.",["t"]="Vengeance from the Grave"}}}}}
t["npc:collin-mauren"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,339,21.458.0,23.439.0,28.460.0,33.142.0,45.245.0,59.174.0,52.200.0,53.201.0,37.218.0",["h"]="dfc0b3",["n"]="Collin Mauren",["s"]="Collin Mauren. Collin Mauren es un mago humano que reside en el Barrio de los Magos, en la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Como erudito investigador y creador de encantamientos, experimenta con componentes naturales exóticos para concebir hechizos de utilidad únicos. Entre sus ocupaciones está ayudar a su conocido, el ingeniero y explorador gnomo Gaxim Silvóxido, con pergaminos arcanos especializados. Ubicado en el bullicioso Barrio de los Magos de Ventormenta, Collin Mauren pasa sus días dedicándose a las aplicaciones más tranquilas y prácticas de la magia. En lugar de perseguir el poder elemental en estado puro, se centra en elaborar fórmulas arcanas que resuelvan problemas logísticos concretos. Collin suele recurrir a anomalías naturales y componentes brutos recolectados por todo Azeroth, entrelazando sus propiedades intrínsecas en pergaminos mágicos funcionales y reactivos tanto para amigos como para viajeros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Collin exemplifies the experimental craft of spell creation, demonstrating how earthly reagents like elemental debris and basilisk scales can be harnessed to weave utility magic.",["faction:Alliance"]="Collin facilitates communication and trade across the Alliance by supplying adventurers with utility magic spanning from Westfall to Kalimdor.",["race:Human"]="Living quietly in Stormwind's Mage Quarter, Collin represents the scholarly pursuits of human wizards who study the broader world from the heart of the capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Collin Mauren is located in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City, tucked among the towers and shops frequented by the capital's arcane scholars.",["al"]={"collin mauren location","where is collin mauren","collin mauren stormwind"},["q"]="Where can Collin Mauren be found?"},{["a"]="Collin specializes in applied enchantments and utility spells. Rather than combat evocations, he experiments with raw natural components—such as elemental debris and beast scales—to devise long-distance messaging scrolls and unique dweomers.",["al"]={"collin mauren research","what does collin mauren do","collin mauren magic"},["q"]="What kind of magic does Collin specialize in?"},{["a"]="Gaxim Rustfizzle is an adventurous gnome tinkerer and a friend of Collin. Collin supports Gaxim's distant journeys by providing him with custom-crafted communication scrolls.",["al"]={"gaxim rustfizzle friend","collin and gaxim","who is gaxim rustfizzle"},["q"]="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle and how is Collin connected to him?"},{["a"]="Collin uses the essence of Westfall's elemental Dust Devils to power a messaging spell. The windy debris of the elementals carries the harmonic energy required to craft reliable communication scrolls.",["al"]={"devils in westfall quest","why dust devils","westfall dust devils quest"},["q"]="Why does Collin need elemental debris from Westfall?"},{["a"]="Collin studies the magical properties of basilisk scales native to the Stonetalon Mountains in Kalimdor. He uses their sturdy, naturally resistant hides as reagent bases to synthesize new incantations.",["al"]={"stonetalon basilisks","retrieval for mauren","stonetalon scales collin"},["q"]="Why is Collin interested in the Stonetalon Mountains?"},{["a"]="While Collin resides in the Mage Quarter and practices the traditions common among Alliance wizards, he functions primarily as an independent researcher and reagent crafter rather than an active Dalaran representative.",["al"]={"is collin kirin tor","collin mauren dalaran","mage quarter collin"},["q"]="Is Collin aligned with the Kirin Tor?"}},["kw"]={"basilisk","collin mauren","dust devils","gaxim rustfizzle","mage quarter","stonetalon","stormwind","westfall"},["n"]="Collin Mauren",["s"]="Collin Mauren is a human mage residing in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind City. A scholarly researcher and crafter of incantations, he experiments with exotic natural reagents to devise unique utility spells. Among his pursuits is assisting his acquaintance, the gnome engineer and explorer Gaxim Rustfizzle, with specialized arcane scrolls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within Stormwind's bustling Mage Quarter, Collin Mauren spends his days pursuing the quieter, more practical applications of magic. Rather than chasing raw elemental power, he focuses on crafting arcane formulas that solve specific, logistical problems. Collin often turns to natural anomalies and raw components scavenged across Azeroth, weaving their intrinsic properties into functional magic scrolls and reagents for friends and travelers alike.",["t"]="Scholar of the Arcane"},{["b"]="Collin maintains a close correspondence and friendship with the gnomish tinker Gaxim Rustfizzle. When Gaxim needed a reliable way to communicate across great distances during his travels, Collin designed a specialized messaging spell. To anchor the spell, he utilizes the whirling debris left behind by Westfall's erratic Dust Devils, capturing the essence of shifting wind to ensure long-distance messages reach his adventurous colleague.",["t"]="Aiding Gaxim Rustfizzle"},{["b"]="Beyond his work with local elementals, Collin's research extends clear across the Great Sea to the crags of Kalimdor. Curiously captivated by the resilient hides of basilisks native to the Stonetalon Mountains, Collin seeks out their scales to synthesize new spells. Travelers venturing into Kalimdor frequently receive his requests for these rare hides, fueling Collin's ongoing fascination with how primal creature anatomy can stabilize complex enchantments.",["t"]="Exotic Studies in Stonetalon"}}}}}
t["npc:cookie"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,336,22.465.0,13.468.0,49.256.0,43.207.0,43.203.0,46.195.0,40.147.0,44.150.0",["h"]="0c079e",["n"]="El Chef",["s"]="El Chef. El Chef es un múrloc de élite que ejerce de cocinero del barco a bordo del acorazado oculto en lo profundo de Las Minas de la Muerte. Un recluta inusual dentro de la Hermandad Defias, cuida los calderos de la tripulación bajo la atenta mirada del Capitán Verdetez y de Edwin VanCleef. Es el único jefe completamente opcional que se encuentra en el dique seco subterráneo. Bajo las cubiertas del imponente acorazado en la Cala del Acorazado, las tareas culinarias no recaen en un batidor humano ni en un ingeniero goblin, sino en un múrloc solitario conocido simplemente como El Chef. La forma en que consiguió el puesto sigue siendo un secreto que solo guarda el mismísimo Edwin VanCleef. Sean cuales sean las dudas que el resto de la tripulación pueda albergar acerca de que un múrloc gestione sus raciones, los piratas rara vez están en posición de ser quisquillosos, y en los bajos fondos de Arroyo de la Luna, comida es comida.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="VanCleef's rogue network relies on strange, unconventional assets, and Cookie proves that even the Brotherhood's supply lines feature odd surprises.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's scouts are often surprised to find murlocs actively working within the Defias leadership rather than merely infesting Westfall's outer shores.",["profession:Cooking"]="Finding a murloc appointed as chief cook aboard an outlaw juggernaut is a testament to the desperate, unrefined standards of pirate cuisine."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Edwin VanCleef is the only one who knows why Cookie was recruited and granted the galley duties. The Defias outlaws and goblin shipwrights simply accept the arrangement because pirate crews take food where they can get it, regardless of the chef's species.",["al"]={"why murloc cook","why is cookie on the ship","cookie defias lore"},["q"]="Why is a murloc working as a cook for the Defias?"},{["a"]="Cookie is located in the Ironclad Cove at the very end of the Deadmines. He patrols the shallow water and docks near the stern of the giant wooden juggernaut, just past the ramp where Mr. Smite stands guard.",["al"]={"where is cookie","cookie location deadmines","finding cookie"},["q"]="Where can Cookie be found in the Deadmines?"},{["a"]="No, Cookie is the only optional boss in the dungeon. Infiltrators can board the vessel directly to confront Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef without ever disturbing the cook's patrol along the shore.",["al"]={"is cookie optional","do you have to kill cookie","cookie skip"},["q"]="Is Cookie required to finish the Deadmines?"},{["a"]="Cookie is not associated with any of the known local murloc tribes, such as those along the Westfall coast. He lives and works entirely among the outlaws and scoundrels of the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"what tribe is cookie","cookie murloc tribe"},["q"]="Does Cookie belong to a specific murloc tribe?"},{["a"]="Cookie wields cooking implements in melee combat and can hurl caustic splashes of acid at attackers, burning them with dangerous culinary mixtures.",["al"]={"cookie abilities","how does cookie fight","cookie attacks"},["q"]="What weapons or attacks does Cookie use?"},{["a"]="Cookie directly serves the naval arm of the Defias Brotherhood under the command of Captain Greenskin, answering ultimately to Edwin VanCleef himself.",["al"]={"cookie boss","who leads cookie","cookie greenskin vancleef"},["q"]="Who does Cookie report to on the juggernaut?"}},["kw"]={"captain greenskin","cook","cookie","deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaut","murloc"},["n"]="Cookie",["s"]="Cookie is an elite murloc serving as the ship's cook aboard the juggernaut hidden deep within the Deadmines. An unusual recruit among the Defias Brotherhood, he tends the crew's cauldrons beneath the watchful eye of Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef. He is the only entirely optional boss encountered within the underground dry dock.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Beneath the decks of the towering juggernaut in the Ironclad Cove, cooking duty falls neither to a human outrider nor a goblin engineer, but to a solitary murloc known simply as Cookie. How he secured the position remains a private secret kept by Edwin VanCleef himself. Whatever doubts the rest of the crew might harbor about a murloc presiding over their rations, pirates are rarely in a position to be picky, and in the underworld of Moonbrook, a meal is a meal.",["t"]="The Brotherhood's Chef"},{["b"]="Cookie patrols the waterways and shores around the pirate flagship, wielding his cooking utensils alongside acidic brews. Despite being isolated from typical murloc tribes, he defends his cauldron with savage ferocity, flinging caustic concoctions at any intruders who wander into the docks. Because his station sits away from the main gangplanks, many who storm the cove bypass his kitchen entirely, making him the only optional overseer aboard the Defias juggernaut.",["t"]="A Bitter Brew"}}}}}
t["npc:corithras-moonrage"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,376,19.376.0,18.389.0,26.394.1,26.211.0,38.125.0,47.222.0,54.273.0,42.167.0,59.168.0",["h"]="caa2d2",["n"]="Coriithas Furia Lunar",["s"]="Coriithas Furia Lunar. Coriithas Furia Lunar es un erudito elfo de la noche y asignador de misiones apostado en la aldea de Dolanaar, en Teldrassil. Guía a los aventureros recién llegados para que comprendan la naturaleza del gran Árbol del Mundo y les encomienda la tarea de mantener sus pozos de la luna sagrados. A través de sus enseñanzas, revela tanto la importancia espiritual de Teldrassil como las crecientes cargas que soportan los kaldorei. Afincado en el sombrío asentamiento de Dolanaar, Coriithas Furia Lunar ejerce de instructor para los viajeros que abandonan los confines protegidos de Cañada Umbría. A medida que los jóvenes kaldorei se adentran en las ramas más extensas de Teldrassil, Coriithas se asegura de que comprendan la historia de su nuevo hogar. Enseña que sobrevivir en esta era cambiante requiere vigilancia y reverencia hacia el orden natural.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids will find Corithras's tasks deeply connected to their calling, as his moonwell rites directly track the health and creeping ailments of the World Tree.",["class:Priest"]="Priests of Elune assist Corithras in carrying the blessed waters of the moonwells, maintaining the spiritual and physical harmony of Dolanaar's surrounding wilds.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, speaking with Corithras is a foundational lesson in the post-Third War reality, confronting the loss of ancient immortality and the disputed creation of Teldrassil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar located in Dolanaar. He introduces adventurers to the history of Teldrassil and tasks them with tending to the sacred moonwells and testing the waters of the World Tree.",["al"]={"corithras moonrage role","who is corithras","dolanaar quest giver"},["q"]="Who is Corithras Moonrage?"},{["a"]="He can be found standing outdoors in Dolanaar, the central crossroads village situated in the southern reaches of Teldrassil.",["al"]={"corithras location","where is corithras","find corithras"},["q"]="Where can Corithras Moonrage be found?"},{["a"]="The Crown of the Earth quests involve drawing water from moonwells across Teldrassil. Corithras combines the collected water for delivery to Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus, where the druids need to replenish their moonwell.",["al"]={"crown of the earth meaning","corithras quests","moonwell quests"},["q"]="What is the Crown of the Earth questline about?"},{["a"]="Corithras shares the history of how Teldrassil was planted after the Third War to restore night elven immortality. Because the Dragon Aspects refused to bless the tree, Corithras remains acutely aware that the tree lacks divine protection and that his people remain mortal.",["al"]={"why burden of kaldorei","aspects refusal","why no immortality"},["q"]="Why is Corithras concerned about Teldrassil's origins?"},{["a"]="He imparts lessons on the recent sacrifices of the Third War, the founding of Teldrassil, and the responsibility each kaldorei bears to defend their new woodland home.",["al"]={"corithras lore","dolanaar history","what does corithras tell you"},["q"]="What does Corithras teach new adventurers?"},{["a"]="He serves as a loyal citizen and scholar of Darnassus in Dolanaar, working closely with druids and priests alike to monitor the well-being of the forest and its waters.",["al"]={"corithras faction","is corithras a druid"},["q"]="Is Corithras aligned with the Cenarion Circle or Darnassus?"}},["kw"]={"corithras moonrage","crown of the earth","dolanaar","fandral staghelm","kaldorei","moonwell","night elf","teldrassil"},["n"]="Corithras Moonrage",["s"]="Corithras Moonrage is a night elf scholar and quest giver stationed in the village of Dolanaar on Teldrassil. He guides newly arrived adventurers in understanding the nature of the great World Tree and tasks them with maintaining its sacred moonwells. Through his lessons, he reveals both the spiritual importance of Teldrassil and the growing burdens carried by the kaldorei.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Residing in the shaded settlement of Dolanaar, Corithras Moonrage serves as an instructor to travelers leaving the sheltered bounds of Shadowglen. As young kaldorei venture into the wider boughs of Teldrassil, Corithras ensures they understand the history of their new home. He teaches that survival in this changing era requires vigilance and reverence for the natural order.",["t"]="Scholar of Dolanaar"},{["b"]="Much of Corithras's duty revolves around collecting moonwell water for the druids in Darnassus. He directs adventurers to collect pure waters from moonwells across Teldrassil in specially crafted phials for delivery to Fandral Staghelm. Through these trials, he monitors the health of the World Tree and seeks to maintain the delicate balance of the wilderness against creeping corruption.",["t"]="Crown of the Earth"},{["b"]="Beneath Corithras's guidance lies an uneasy truth regarding Teldrassil's creation. Unlike the ancient Nordrassil, this new World Tree was raised without the blessings of the Dragon Aspects, who refused Fandral Staghelm's ambitious creation. Corithras reflects on the loss of night elven immortality and the fragile, uncertain future the kaldorei now face under the boughs of an unblessed bough.",["t"]="The Burden of the Kaldorei"}}}}}
t["npc:dalar-dawnweaver"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,419,17.525.0,32.503.0,24.268.0,42.265.0,40.245.0,46.275.0,45.248.0,36.186.0",["h"]="7e4143",["n"]="Dalar Tejalba",["s"]="Dalar Tejalba. Dalar Tejalba es un antiguo archimago de Dalaran que ahora sirve a los Renegados en El Sepulcro, en el Bosque de Argénteos. Asesinado durante la destrucción de la ciudad de los magos a manos de la Plaga y liberado más tarde del control del Rey Exánime, enfoca su intelecto mágico en analizar las amenazas regionales. Desde las sombras de la tumba, dirige los esfuerzos para comprender la persistente presencia de Dalaran y poner fin a la locura del archimago Arugal. En vida, Dalar Tejalba ostentaba un alto rango en el Kirin Tor y recorría las estancias de la Ciudadela Violeta cuando Dalaran era la cumbre del dominio arcano. Su vida mortal llegó a su fin cuando la Plaga saqueó la ciudad para preparar la invocación de Archimonde. Reanimado como un siervo descerebrado del Rey Exánime, Dalar se liberó junto a Lady Sylvanas Brisaveloz cuando el dominio de la Plaga decayó. Ahora apostado en El Sepulcro, conserva el agudo intelecto de un archimago, volcado por completo en proteger el reino de los Renegados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Forsaken mages will find in Dalar a dark mirror of Dalaran's former grandeur, demonstrating how Kirin Tor training can be weaponized in service to the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="Stationed at the Sepulcher, Dalar secures the Horde's western frontier by coordinating strikes against the worgen of Shadowfang Keep and hostile Kirin Tor enclaves.",["race:Undead"]="Dalar exemplifies the reclaimed agency of the Forsaken, turning the very knowledge he possessed in life against Dalaran remnants and rogue wizards who threaten their sovereignty."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dalar Dawnweaver is a Forsaken mage found at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. In life, he was an archmage of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. After dying during the Third War and being raised by the Scourge, he broke free of the Lich King's control to serve the Dark Lady.",["al"]={"who is dalar","dalar dawnweaver lore","dalar background"},["q"]="Who is Dalar Dawnweaver?"},{["a"]="Dalar was present in Dalaran when Arthas Menethil and the Scourge invaded to recover the Book of Medivh. Slain during the assault as Kel'Thuzad summoned Archimonde into Azeroth, Dalar was raised into undeath as a servant of the Scourge until Sylvanas liberated him.",["al"]={"how did dalar die","dalar death","dalar third war"},["q"]="What happened to him during the Third War?"},{["a"]="He serves as the local arcane authority for the Forsaken in Silverpine Forest. His historical familiarity with both the Kirin Tor forces occupying Ambermill and his former peer, Archmage Arugal, makes him ideally suited to counter those threats.",["al"]={"why is dalar in sepulcher","dalar role in silverpine"},["q"]="Why is Dalar stationed at the Sepulcher?"},{["a"]="Both were mages of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran before its fall. Dalar recognizes the tragic descent and lethal danger of Arugal's summoning experiments in Shadowfang Keep, tasking adventurers with gathering relics of Arugal's folly and ultimately demanding the mad mage's death.",["al"]={"dalar and arugal","did dalar know arugal"},["q"]="What is Dalar's connection to Archmage Arugal?"},{["a"]="Dalar keeps a watchful eye on his former homeland and the surviving Kirin Tor forces stationed at Ambermill. He directs agents to intercept their communications and analyze their intentions to ensure they cannot threaten the Forsaken in Silverpine.",["al"]={"dalar and dalaran","dalar ambermill"},["q"]="What does Dalar want with Dalaran's remnants?"},{["a"]="No. While he was once an archmage among them, his loyalty now lies with the Forsaken and the Horde. He actively opposes the surviving Kirin Tor forces operating within Silverpine Forest.",["al"]={"is dalar kirin tor","is dalar loyal to dalaran"},["q"]="Is Dalar aligned with the Kirin Tor?"}},["kw"]={"archmage","arugal","dalar","dalaran","dawnweaver","forsaken","kirin tor","sepulcher","silverpine"},["n"]="Dalar Dawnweaver",["s"]="Dalar Dawnweaver is a former archmage of Dalaran who now serves the Forsaken at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Slain during the Scourge's destruction of the magi's city and later freed from the Lich King's control, he turns his magical intellect toward dissecting regional threats. From the shadows of the tomb, he directs efforts to understand Dalaran's lingering presence and undo the madness of Archmage Arugal.",["sec"]={{["b"]="In life, Dalar Dawnweaver held high rank among the Kirin Tor, walking the halls of the Violet Citadel when Dalaran was a pinnacle of arcane mastery. His mortal life ended when the Scourge sacked the city to pave the way for Archimonde's summoning. Reanimated into the mindless thrall of the Lich King, Dalar broke free alongside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner when the Scourge's grip faltered. Now stationed at the Sepulcher, he retains the piercing intellect of an archmage, turned entirely toward safeguarding the Forsaken realm.",["t"]="A Fallen Archmage"},{["b"]="Silverpine Forest is caught between multiple perils, and Dalar serves as the Sepulcher's arcane strategist. To the south, Dalaran wizards occupy Ambermill under a protective dome, meddling in matters Dalar seeks to uncover and disrupt. Even closer looms Shadowfang Keep and the feral worgen loosed upon the woods. Dalar possesses intimate knowledge of his former colleague, Archmage Arugal, and meticulously orchestrates campaigns to neutralize Arugal's beastly creations before they overrun the region.",["t"]="Eyes on Ambermill and Shadowfang"}}}}}
t["npc:daphne-stilwell"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,287,20.475.0,21.485.0,18.451.1,23.211.0,27.183.0,51.248.0,40.226.0,26.163.0,31.157.0",["h"]="640164",["n"]="Daphne Fontana",["s"]="Daphne Fontana. Daphne Fontana cuida de un huerto aislado en lo alto de los acantilados costeros de Páramos de Poniente con vistas a Playa Larga. Junto a su esposo Jordan, huyó del caos del norte y se trasladó al sur, colaborando discretamente con la Iglesia de la Luz Sagrada mientras defiende su hogar de los forajidos de los alrededores. Encaramada a los riscos al oeste de Arroyo de la Luna y la salida de Las Minas de la Muerte, Daphne Fontana regenta una granja y un huerto de manzanos retirados. Desde abajo, a lo largo de Playa Larga, o desde arriba en las rutas de grifos hacia el sur rumbo a la Vega de Tuercespina, la pequeña granja parece tranquila y modesta. Sin embargo, llevar una hacienda en los Páramos de Poniente actuales dista mucho de ser seguro. A pesar del asedio de los bandidos y los carroñeros errantes, Daphne trabaja con esmero sus árboles y vigila su aislado pedazo de tierra.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Daphne Stilwell is a vital figure in the trials of the Tome of Valor; defending her from ruthless Defias marauders proves a paladin's devotion to protecting the innocent.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Stilwells embody the plight of displaced northern refugees who continue to serve the Alliance and the Church of the Holy Light despite the perils of the Westfall frontier."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Daphne Stilwell is a human homesteader living in an isolated farmhouse above Westfall's Longshore. She is the wife of the famed blacksmith Jordan Stilwell, with whom she escaped the devastated northern kingdoms.",["al"]={"who is daphne","daphne stilwell info","stilwell wife"},["q"]="Who is Daphne Stilwell?"},{["a"]="Daphne previously lived in the north near Pyrewood Village and worked at what is now known as Shadowfang Keep before calamity drove her and Jordan southward to the lands of Stormwind.",["al"]={"daphne origin","where is daphne from","is daphne gilnean"},["q"]="Where did Daphne come from?"},{["a"]="Her farm sits on the cliffs directly overlooking the southern waters of Westfall, right above the exit tunnels of the Deadmines. Its proximity to the Defias stronghold makes it an easy target for outlaws looking to raid supplies or remove meddlers.",["al"]={"why do defias attack daphne","defias farm attack","stilwell farm bandits"},["q"]="Why is her farm attacked by the Defias Brotherhood?"},{["a"]="Her husband Jordan aids the Church of the Holy Light by forging sanctified weapons. As part of their trials for the Tome of Valor, paladins of the Silver Hand are dispatched to Westfall to safeguard Daphne from bandit attacks.",["al"]={"paladin quest daphne","tome of valor daphne","why do paladins visit daphne"},["q"]="What is Daphne's connection to paladins?"},{["a"]="Yes. When the Defias assault her orchard, she does not cower; she draws a weapon and directly battles the attackers alongside any paladins defending the homestead.",["al"]={"does daphne fight","is daphne a warrior"},["q"]="Can Daphne defend herself?"},{["a"]="Her farm is tucked on the clifftops of south-western Westfall, situated southwest of Moonbrook near the Deadmines secret cove exit overlooking the Longshore.",["al"]={"where is daphne farm","how to get to stilwell farm","daphne stilwell location"},["q"]="How do you reach her farmhouse?"}},["kw"]={"daphne stilwell","defias brotherhood","jordan stilwell","longshore","orchard","pyrewood village","shadowfang keep","tome of valor","westfall"},["n"]="Daphne Stilwell",["s"]="Daphne Stilwell tends an isolated orchard nestled atop the coastal cliffs of Westfall overlooking the Longshore. Together with her husband Jordan, she fled turmoil in the north and relocated south, quietly aiding the Church of the Holy Light while defending her home from nearby outlaws.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on the bluffs to the west of Moonbrook and the exit of the Deadmines, Daphne Stilwell manages a secluded homestead and apple orchard. From below along the Longshore or above on gryphon routes south to Stranglethorn Vale, the small farm looks quiet and unassuming. Yet running a homestead in modern Westfall is anything but safe. Despite the encroaching bandits and roaming scavengers, Daphne diligently works her trees and keeps watch over her isolated patch of land.",["t"]="A Life on the Cliffs"},{["b"]="Before settling in the hills of Westfall, Daphne and her husband Jordan lived in Lordaeron near Pyrewood Village, working in what is now Shadowfang Keep. When darkness and disaster overtook the region, they were driven southward along with thousands of other human refugees. In Stormwind's orbit, Jordan's renowned craftsmanship and Daphne's steady presence led them to forge close ties with the Church of the Holy Light, providing support and holy arms to paladins of the Silver Hand.",["t"]="Refugees of the North"},{["b"]="Living so close to the Deadmines puts Daphne square in the path of the Defias Brotherhood. While Jordan travels or labors on forging holy weaponry outside the capital, Daphne is frequently left to maintain their coastal home alone. When brigands raided the farmstead seeking retribution or plunder, Daphne picked up arms and fought alongside aspiring paladins sent by the Cathedral, proving herself remarkably fierce and capable in the heat of battle.",["t"]="Defending the Farm"}}}}}
t["npc:darsok-swiftdagger"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,370,27.449.0,24.425.1,24.426.0,36.164.0,30.202.0,27.182.0,52.205.0,48.147.0,36.165.0",["h"]="3128f3",["n"]="Darsok Movedaga",["s"]="Darsok Movedaga. Darsok Movedaga es un guerrero y explorador orco apostado en El Cruce, en pleno corazón de Los Baldíos. Conocido por su feroz odio hacia las arpías, dirige a los aventureros de la Horda hacia el norte, a Las Colinas Áridas, para desarticular el matriarcado aviar que hostiga a viajeros y asentamientos. Mantiene contactos por todas las llanuras y actúa como un intermediario de confianza para el médico brujo Jin'Zil en Malaka'jin. En medio del bullicioso enclave de El Cruce, Darsok Movedaga vigila atentamente las amenazas que surgen del matorral septentrional. La arteria comercial que conecta Durotar, Mulgore y las regiones del norte se encuentra bajo un asedio constante, no solo por parte de saqueadores y centauros, sino también de cazadoras aéreas organizadas. Darsok concentra su ira en las arpías Alabruja, cuyos nidos en Las Colinas Áridas, al noroeste de Las Charcas del Olvido, amenazan directamente a las caravanas del norte.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Living up to the name Swiftdagger, Darsok favors precise, lethal decapitation strikes against enemy leadership rather than grinding attrition.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde travelers, Darsok provides crucial early tactical missions that secure the crossroads trade routes against aerial ambush.",["race:Orc"]="Darsok exemplifies the focused, martial mindset of orcs tasked with taming and securing Kalimdor's perilous frontier."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Darsok Swiftdagger is stationed in the Crossroads, the central Horde settlement in the Barrens. He stands ready to direct passing travelers toward northern threats.",["al"]={"darsok location","where is darsok swiftdagger","find darsok","darsok swiftdagger spot"},["q"]="Where is Darsok Swiftdagger located?"},{["a"]="The Witchwing harpies roost in the canyons northwest of the Forgotten Pools and pose a constant predatory danger to Horde caravans, travelers, and scouts moving along the northern trails of the Barrens.",["al"]={"why kill harpies","darsok harpy grudge","witchwing harpies barrens"},["q"]="Why is Darsok hunting harpies?"},{["a"]="Serena Bloodfeather is the cruel matriarch leading the Witchwing harpies of the Dry Hills. Darsok tasks adventurers with slaying her to shatter the cohesion and command of the flock.",["al"]={"serena bloodfeather","harpy leader barrens","witchwing leader"},["q"]="Who is Serena Bloodfeather?"},{["a"]="Darsok is an ally and correspondent of Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, a Darkspear troll stationed at Malaka'jin. He facilitates communications and sends adventurers carrying missives to Jin'Zil's remote encampment.",["al"]={"jin'zil letter","darsok and jin'zil","witch doctor jin'zil connection"},["q"]="What is Darsok's connection to Witch Doctor Jin'Zil?"},{["a"]="Darsok organizes his harpy campaign from the Crossroads. No Classic source here identifies either Sergra Darkthorn or Thork as his direct superior.",["al"]={"darsok thork","who does darsok answer to","crossroads leadership"},["q"]="Does Darsok report to Sergra Darkthorn or Thork?"},{["a"]="The Witchwing harpies roost in the Dry Hills, a series of jagged ravines and cliffs situated northwest of the Forgotten Pools in the northern reaches of the Barrens.",["al"]={"witchwing location","dry hills harpies","where to find harpies barrens"},["q"]="Where do the Witchwing harpies nest?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","bloodfeather","crossroads","darsok","harpy","jin'zil","serena","swiftdagger","thork","witchwing"},["n"]="Darsok Swiftdagger",["s"]="Darsok Swiftdagger is an orc warrior and scout stationed at the Crossroads in the heart of the Barrens. Known for his fierce hatred of harpies, he directs Horde adventurers north into the Dry Hills to break the avian matriarchy harassing travelers and settlements. He maintains ties across the plains, serving as a trusted contact for Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in Malaka'jin.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Amid the bustling hub of the Crossroads, Darsok Swiftdagger keeps a sharp eye on the threats creeping out of the northern scrubland. The trade artery connecting Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern reaches is under constant siege, not only from raiders and centaur, but from organized aerial hunters. Darsok focuses his wrath on the Witchwing harpies, whose roosts in the Dry Hills northwest of the Forgotten Pools directly threaten northern caravans.",["t"]="A Watcher at the Crossroads"},{["b"]="Darsok does not merely defend the roads; he coordinates targeted strikes deep into harpy territory. His campaign begins by thinning the aggressive Harpy Raiders before tasking hardened fighters with executing lieutenants and ultimately taking the head of their matriarch, Serena Bloodfeather. By systematically dismantling their leadership, Swiftdagger aims to leave the predatory flock broken and scattered across the crags.",["t"]="The War on the Witchwing"},{["b"]="While his immediate duties center around harpy eradication, Darsok Swiftdagger serves as an important point of contact within the Horde network. He maintains correspondence with Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, the enigmatic troll residing at Malaka'jin on the border of the Stonetalon Mountains. Messages and intelligence carried through Darsok help ensure that outlying enclaves stay informed of developments across the central plains.",["t"]="Connections in the Scrub"}}}}}
t["npc:deathguard-dillinger"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,251,17.361.0,24.352.0,27.354.1,38.121.0,35.205.0,43.199.0,44.153.0,54.220.0,24.189.0",["h"]="de7793",["n"]="Guardia de la Muerte Dillinger",["s"]="Guardia de la Muerte Dillinger. El Guardia de la Muerte Dillinger es un centinela Renegado apostado en Rémol, en los Claros de Tirisfal. Vigilando el perímetro de la villa, orienta a los no-muertos recién llegados hacia los servicios necesarios y encomienda a los reclutas la tarea de mantener a raya a los restos locales de la Plaga. Como miembro de la Guardia de la Muerte de los Renegados, Dillinger hace guardia a la entrada de Rémol, sirviendo tanto de protector de primera línea como de guía de orientación para los viajeros que salen de Camposanto. Proporciona indicaciones hacia los servicios del pueblo, como la posada, el ayuntamiento y los instructores locales, ayudando a los no-muertos recién despertados a orientarse en su nueva realidad bajo el mandato de la Dama Oscura.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Aspiring Forsaken warriors frequently work directly with Dillinger to test their martial mettle against the ferocious ghouls and skeletal horrors prowling the outskirts of Brill.",["faction:Horde"]="Dillinger represents the Forsaken's struggle to carve out a secure foothold in northern Lordaeron, showing Horde allies the relentless menace posed by mindless Scourge at their doorsteps.",["race:Undead"]="For newly freed Forsaken arriving from Deathknell, Dillinger is often the first face of military authority they meet, directing them toward training and their first duties in service of Sylvanas."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Deathguard Dillinger is posted on the outskirts of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades, watching the path leading into town.",["al"]={"dillinger location","where is dillinger","deathguard dillinger coordinates"},["q"]="Where can I find Deathguard Dillinger?"},{["a"]="The Deathguard serves as the military standing army and constabulary of the Forsaken, guarding settlements like Brill and the Undercity against the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and other regional threats.",["al"]={"what is deathguard","who are the deathguards","deathguard purpose"},["q"]="What is the role of the Deathguard?"},{["a"]="Dillinger tasks adventurers with slaying mindless Scourge wandering the surrounding fields and mills, reclaiming vital local infrastructure, and dealing with dangerous entities like Ulag the Cleaver.",["al"]={"dillinger quests","what quests does dillinger have"},["q"]="What tasks does Deathguard Dillinger offer?"},{["a"]="Yes, speaking with Dillinger allows players to request directions to essential services, profession trainers, and class mentors located throughout Brill.",["al"]={"dillinger directions","ask dillinger for help"},["q"]="Can Deathguard Dillinger provide directions?"},{["a"]="The mindless undead wandering Tirisfal remain under the thrall of the Scourge and the Lich King. Having broken free of that mental control, the Forsaken must eliminate these feral remnants to protect their own territory.",["al"]={"why fight scourge","undead fighting undead","brill ghouls"},["q"]="Why are the Forsaken fighting other undead near Brill?"},{["a"]="Ulag the Cleaver is a dangerous Scourge horror tied to nearby tombs outside Brill. Dillinger coordinates with Forsaken recruits to summon and destroy Ulag to keep the surrounding area safe.",["al"]={"ulag quest","who is ulag","ulag the cleaver"},["q"]="Who is Ulag the Cleaver?"}},["kw"]={"a putrid task","brill","deathguard","deathguard dillinger","dillinger","the mills overrun","tirisfal glades","ulag the cleaver"},["n"]="Deathguard Dillinger",["s"]="Deathguard Dillinger is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Brill within Tirisfal Glades. Standing watch over the town's perimeter, he directs newly arrived undead toward necessary services and tasks recruits with keeping the local Scourge remnants at bay.",["sec"]={{["b"]="As a member of the Forsaken Deathguard, Dillinger stands at the entrance of Brill, serving as both a frontline protector and an orienting guide for travelers emerging from Deathknell. He provides directions to town amenities such as the inn, the town hall, and local trainers, helping newly awakened undead navigate their new reality under the Dark Lady's rule.",["t"]="Sentinel of Brill"},{["b"]="Dillinger actively enlists capable adventurers to purge lingering mindless Scourge from the nearby farms and mills. Through assignments like cullling rotting ghouls and reclaiming infested facilities, he seeks to establish a buffer zone of security around Brill, ensuring the fledgling Forsaken settlements can endure against unending undead predation.",["t"]="Securing the Borderlands"},{["b"]="Beyond routine patrols, Dillinger coordinates responses against persistent Scourge threats lurking in the ruins around Brill. When summoned horrors such as Ulag the Cleaver emerge from nearby tombs or neglected homesteads, Dillinger ensures able fighters are dispatched to put the rampaging monstrosities down before they breach the settlement's borders.",["t"]="Containing Mindless Horrors"}}}}}
t["npc:delgren-the-purifier"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,326,35.474.0,23.449.1,18.429.0,28.276.0,25.142.0,52.228.0,55.246.0,29.170.0,45.194.0",["h"]="6a54f2",["n"]="Delgren el Purificador",["s"]="Delgren el Purificador. Delgren el Purificador es un paladín humano apostado en la Atalaya de Maestra, en el extremo norte de Vallefresno. Junto a sus camaradas Balthule Golpesombra y Feero Ferramán, ayuda a los elfos de la noche a purgar la magia demoníaca y la Magia de las Sombras que amenazan la frontera, centrándose en particular en el siniestro Culto de la Facción Oscura. Los paladines humanos son una visión poco común en las profundidades de los antiguos bosques de Kalimdor, pero Delgren el Purificador llegó con una misión. Vinculado al Alba Argenta, Delgren viajó hacia el oeste con un destacamento de guerreros sagrados decididos a prestar ayuda a los nuevos aliados elfos de la noche de la Alianza frente a los males residuales de demonios y vestigios de no-muertos de la Tercera Guerra. Apostado cerca de la frontera entre Costa Oscura y Vallefresno, mantiene una constante vigilancia sobre los viajeros que avanzan hacia el sur desde Auberdine.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Delgren represents the far reach of the Holy Light on Kalimdor, demonstrating how paladins adapt their crusade against demons and dark magic far beyond the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers heading south from Darkshore, Delgren and his companions provide a reassuring military foothold along the dangerous Ashenvale road.",["race:NightElf"]="Though traditional kaldorei are often skeptical of foreign creeds, Delgren's company has earned trust through their practical crusade against the demonic cults troubling ancient ruins."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Delgren is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post along the road in northern Ashenvale. As an agent of the Argent Dawn, he assists the night elves in defending their lands from demonic corruption, cultists, and lingering shadows left in the wake of the Legion's invasion.",["al"]={"who is delgren","delgren lore","who is the paladin at maestras post"},["q"]="Who is Delgren the Purifier?"},{["a"]="Delgren stands at Maestra's Post, a small night elven outpost in northwestern Ashenvale just south of the border trail leading into Darkshore.",["al"]={"where is delgren","delgren location","delgren coordinates"},["q"]="Where can I find Delgren?"},{["a"]="Delgren journeyed west with a company of Argent Dawn paladins to offer aid to the Alliance's night elven allies. Their purpose is to help purge demonic incursions, undead remnants, and dark cults that threaten northern Kalimdor.",["al"]={"why is delgren in ashenvale","why are there humans in ashenvale","delgren mission"},["q"]="Why is a human paladin all the way out in Ashenvale?"},{["a"]="Delgren and his companions monitor the corrupt activities radiating from the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. He directs adventurers to investigate the ruin, hunt the Cult of the Dark Strand, and dismantle their dark summoning practices.",["al"]={"delgren althalaxx","tower of althalaxx quests","cult of the dark strand"},["q"]="What is Delgren's connection to the Tower of Althalaxx?"},{["a"]="Delgren learned Orcish to better comprehend the situation and inhabitants of Kalimdor, a decision that earned him notable disapproval from his superiors within the order.",["al"]={"delgren speaks orcish","does delgren speak orcish","delgren orc language"},["q"]="Why did Delgren learn Orcish?"},{["a"]="He operates alongside Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand, working as a coordinated unit to monitor border threats, handle logistics, and purge shadow cultists along the Ashenvale frontier.",["al"]={"delgren companions","who is at maestras post"},["q"]="Who does Delgren work with at Maestra's Post?"}},["kw"]={"althalaxx","argent dawn","ashenvale","balthule shadowstrike","cult of the dark strand","delgren","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post","tower of althalaxx"},["n"]="Delgren the Purifier",["s"]="Delgren the Purifier is a human paladin stationed at Maestra's Post on the northern edge of Ashenvale. Operating alongside comrades Balthule Shadowstrike and Feero Ironhand, he aids the night elves in cleansing demonic and shadow magic threatening the frontier, with a particular focus on the sinister Cult of the Dark Strand.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Human paladins are a rare sight deep within the ancient forests of Kalimdor, but Delgren the Purifier arrived with a mission. Affiliated with the Argent Dawn, Delgren traveled west with a cadre of holy warriors determined to assist the Alliance's new night elf allies against the lingering evils of demons and undead remnants from the Third War. Stationed near the border of Darkshore and Ashenvale, he maintains a watchful vigil over travelers passing south from Auberdine.",["t"]="A Crusader on the Kaldorei Frontier"},{["b"]="Delgren's immediate crusade pits him directly against the Cult of the Dark Strand, a malevolent cabal operating around the Tower of Althalaxx in northern Darkshore. Teaming with the scout Balthule Shadowstrike, Delgren orchestrates strikes into the cult's territory, investigating their dark rituals and sending adventurers to strike down cultists, shatter their summoning focuses, and root out corrupt warlocks who dare traffic with demonic shadow.",["t"]="Purging the Dark Strand"},{["b"]="Despite his fierce devotion to the Holy Light and zealous nickname, Delgren possesses an unusual perspective on Kalimdor's tangled politics. Much to the annoyance and disdain of his conservative superiors, he took the time to learn Orcish. This rare linguistic skill hints at an unconventional mind—one that seeks to understand the enemies and neighbors sharing this untamed continent rather than relying solely on blind dogma.",["t"]="An Unorthodox Mind"}}}}}
t["npc:denalan"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,412,27.520.0,36.526.0,25.205.0,44.296.0,41.311.0,42.250.0,27.212.0,52.236.0",["h"]="4c952e",["n"]="Denalan",["s"]="Denalan. Denalan es un consumado herborista y botánico elfo de la noche que cuida de una tranquila parcela junto a la orilla oriental del Lago Al'Ameth. Al abrigo de un modesto toldo, consagra sus días al estudio de la flora de la isla y a buscar remedios botánicos para la extraña corrupción que aqueja a Teldrassil. A menudo recurre a jóvenes aventureros para recolectar muestras, estudiar a los violentos brezomaderas y probar tierras encantadas. Mientras muchos kaldorei se centran en la vigilancia marcial o en los grandes ritos druídicos, Denalan cultiva el paciente y meticuloso oficio de la botánica. Asentado en las serenas orillas orientales del Lago Al'Ameth, ha levantado un modesto campamento de investigación provisto de un toldo de tela, aperos sencillos y ordenadas hileras de jardineras de cultivo. En vez de retirarse a los majestuosos túmulos de Darnassus, prefiere permanecer pegado a la tierra para examinar de primera mano la insólita vegetación que ha brotado tras la plantación del nuevo Árbol del Mundo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids will find common cause with Denalan's lakeside experiments, as his work directly assists the Cenarion Circle's efforts to trace and purge the taint spreading through Teldrassil's roots.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Denalan exemplifies the kaldorei tradition of botanical study, demonstrating how gathering and cultivating wild plants can diagnose deeper ailments in the natural world.",["race:NightElf"]="Denalan's research at Lake Al'Ameth represents early kaldorei attempts to understand the unexpected flaws and growing pains of their new home, Teldrassil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Denalan is located on the eastern bank of Lake Al'Ameth in southern Teldrassil, south of Dolanaar. He maintains a small camp with an awning and several cultivated planting beds right near the water's edge.",["al"]={"denalan location","where is denalan","denalan map"},["q"]="Where can I find Denalan?"},{["a"]="Denalan is an herbalist studying the unusual flora of Teldrassil and the aggressive behavior of local woodland spirits. He uses enchanted planter boxes to grow timberling seeds, analyze curious wild plant specimens, and find ways to cleanse corruption seeping into the new World Tree's ecosystem.",["al"]={"what does denalan do","denalan purpose","why is denalan at the lake"},["q"]="What is Denalan researching at his campsite?"},{["a"]="Timberlings are plant-like nature spirits native to the boughs of Teldrassil. Normally peaceful parts of the forest ecology, they have become violent and erratic due to an unnatural corruption spreading through the soil and roots of the World Tree, prompting researchers like Denalan to investigate their seeds.",["al"]={"why are timberlings aggressive","timberling lore","corrupted timberlings"},["q"]="Why are the timberlings attacking people?"},{["a"]="Denalan keeps specially prepared planter beds filled with enchanted earth. He uses them to cultivate wild seeds and strange botanical cuttings, allowing him to safely observe how the forest's flora reacts to purified soil away from wild contaminants.",["al"]={"denalan planter","denalans earth","denalan dirt boxes"},["q"]="What are Denalan's planter boxes used for?"},{["a"]="Denalan has worked closely with fellow herbalists such as Sylvia Whisperbloom and stays in regular communication with druidic researchers and scholars across Teldrassil, including Rellian Greenspyre in Darnassus.",["al"]={"denalan allies","who does denalan report to"},["q"]="Who does Denalan work with?"},{["a"]="The Moss-twined Heart is a blighted botanical core recovered from Blackmoss the Fetid, a corrupted timberling in Teldrassil. Denalan studies it in his enchanted soil to understand the unnatural sickness twisting the island's plant life.",["al"]={"moss twined heart","moss-twined heart quest","blackmoss heart"},["q"]="What is the Moss-twined Heart that Denalan examines?"}},["kw"]={"blackmoss","botany","denalan","herbalist","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","planter","teldrassil","timberlings"},["n"]="Denalan",["s"]="Denalan is an accomplished night elf herbalist and botanist who tends a quiet lakeside plot along the eastern shore of Lake Al'Ameth. Working under a simple awning, he devotes his days to studying the island's plant life and seeking botanical remedies for the strange corruption affecting Teldrassil. He frequently enlists young adventurers to gather samples, study violent timberlings, and test enchanted soils.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While many kaldorei focus on martial vigilance or high druidic rites, Denalan pursues the patient, meticulous craft of herbalism. Stationed along the tranquil eastern banks of Lake Al'Ameth, he has established a modest research camp consisting of a cloth awning, simple field tools, and tidy rows of cultivated planter boxes. Rather than retreating to the grand barrows of Darnassus, he prefers to remain close to the loam, directly examining the unusual flora that has sprouted since the planting of the new World Tree.",["t"]="A Botanist at Lake Al'Ameth"},{["b"]="Denalan's research is far more than an academic curiosity; it addresses the growing unrest among Teldrassil's native wildlife. The timberlings, normally docile woodland beings of wood and sprout, have turned increasingly aggressive. Denalan enchants specialized soil to nurse wild seeds in captivity and analyze how malignant forces seep into the root systems. By studying strange specimens like shimmering fronds, glowing fruit, and moss-twined growths, he seeks to isolate whatever dark taint is troubling the forest boughs.",["t"]="Investigating Teldrassil's Blemishes"}}}}}
t["npc:dendrite-starblaze"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,368,27.425.0,18.422.0,26.175.0,40.246.0,42.189.0,38.107.0,54.202.0,44.165.0",["h"]="6d16a8",["n"]="Dendrite Rafagaestelar",["s"]="Dendrite Rafagaestelar. Dendrite Rafagaestelar es un druida elfo de la noche que reside en la aldea sagrada de Amparo de la Noche, en Claro de la Luna. Al servicio del Círculo Cenarion, actúa como un mentor y guía esencial para los druidas noveles, tanto elfos de la noche como tauren. A través de él, los practicantes son convocados a la arboleda sagrada para dominar ritos fundamentales como la purificación de toxinas y la comunión con las formas de la naturaleza. Ubicado en Amparo de la Noche, Dendrite Rafagaestelar representa el espíritu neutral y duradero del Círculo Cenarion. Cuando los druidas novatos aprenden a sintonizar sus espíritus con Teletransporte a: Claro de la Luna, Dendrite se encuentra entre los primeros en darles la bienvenida a su llegada. Une la antigua tradición kaldorei con la senda emergente de los tauren, tratando a todos los que escuchan la llamada de la naturaleza como hermanos bajo las ramas del sagrado refugio.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Dendrite Starblaze is one of your principal guides upon first teleporting to Moonglade, instructing you in curing sickness and pursuing aquatic forms.",["race:NightElf"]="Dendrite preserves the classical rites of Kaldorei nature stewardship, welcoming Kaldorei initiates into the Cenarion order at Nighthaven.",["race:Tauren"]="For Shu'halo druids visiting Moonglade from Mulgore, Dendrite serves as living proof that the Cenarion Circle's bond transcends the feud between the Horde and the Alliance."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dendrite Starblaze is a night elf druid and Cenarion Circle mentor located in Nighthaven within Moonglade. He guides developing druids through vital class trials and training.",["al"]={"dendrite starblaze","who is dendrite","starblaze moonglade"},["q"]="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?"},{["a"]="The Cenarion Circle stands outside the political factions of the Alliance and Horde. In Moonglade, night elves and tauren practice the druidic arts together under ancient oaths of brotherhood, leaving worldly conflicts beyond the mountain passes.",["al"]={"why does dendrite train horde","dendrite tauren druid","cross faction druid mentor"},["q"]="Why does a night elf train Horde tauren?"},{["a"]="Dendrite oversees several foundational druid class trials. These include quests to master venom and disease curing, as well as trials leading toward the communion required for aquatic form.",["al"]={"dendrite quests","starblaze quest list"},["q"]="What quests does Dendrite Starblaze offer?"},{["a"]="He is located in Nighthaven, the settlement situated on the northern shores of Lake Elune'ara in Moonglade.",["al"]={"dendrite location","where is starblaze","dendrite starblaze map"},["q"]="Where can Dendrite Starblaze be found?"},{["a"]="Novice druids are taught the spell Teleport: Moonglade by their racial trainers around their tenth circle of training. Casting this sends them directly to Moonglade, where Dendrite awaits their arrival.",["al"]={"how to get to dendrite","teleport to moonglade quest"},["q"]="How do young druids reach Dendrite for the first time?"},{["a"]="Non-druids can visit Nighthaven and speak with Dendrite, but he does not offer training, trials, or quests to those outside the Cenarion Circle's druidic traditions.",["al"]={"non druid dendrite","can warrior talk to starblaze"},["q"]="Can non-druid adventurers interact with him?"}},["kw"]={"aquatic form","cenarion circle","curing the sick","dendrite starblaze","druid","lessons anew","moonglade","night elf","nighthaven"},["n"]="Dendrite Starblaze",["s"]="Dendrite Starblaze is a night elf druid residing in the sacred village of Nighthaven within Moonglade. Serving the Cenarion Circle, he acts as a vital mentor and guide for budding druids of both night elf and tauren descent. Through him, practitioners are summoned to the holy grove to master essential rites such as cleansing toxins and communing with nature's forms.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched within Nighthaven, Dendrite Starblaze represents the nonpartisan, enduring spirit of the Cenarion Circle. When novice druids learn to attune their spirits to Teleport: Moonglade, Dendrite is among the first to welcome them upon arrival. He bridges the gap between ancient Kaldorei tradition and the emerging path of the tauren, treating all who heed the call of the wild as kin beneath the boughs of the sacred haven.",["t"]="A Guide in the Sacred Haven"},{["b"]="Dendrite's primary duty involves initiating druidic apprentices into the deeper mysteries of nature. He directs novices through the trials required to understand poison and pestilence, sending them to examine tainted waters and discover herbal curatives. He also oversees the steps that lead druids to the water trials, testing their patience and endurance beneath the surface before granting communion with aquatic forms.",["t"]="Trials of the Wild"}}}}}
